    ; dcterms:source "Guyton1972_Angiotensin MODEL0911342562 (MDFLW -> ANGSCR, decreasing): higher renal/MD flow suppresses renin secretion | textbook corroboration: OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-098 (17.11: Organs with Secondary Endocrine Functions): 'A decline in blood flow to the kidneys stimulates them to release the enzyme renin, triggering the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone (RAAS) system'; OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-114 (20.5: Homeostatic Regulation of the Vascular System): 'Specialized cells in the kidneys, called juxtaglomerular (JG) cells, respond to decreased blood pressure by secreting renin into the blood.'"
    ; pmo:mechanism "renal baroreceptor + macula densa (tubuloglomerular) feedback"
    .
