<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Apah_enzyme_activity%3Apositive%3Aplasma_tyrosine> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/pah_enzyme_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_tyrosine> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry Ch. 18 (tyrosine is the PAH product; becomes dietarily essential in PKU); PKU OMIM 261600 | textbook corroboration: OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-141 (24.5: Protein Metabolism): 'People afflicted with PKU lack sufficient activity of the enzyme phenylalanine hydroxylase and are therefore unable to break down phenylalanine into tyrosine adequately' — PAH converts Phe to Tyr, so reduced PAH lowers plasma tyrosine; Wong, Cells: Molecules and Mechanisms §wong-6.7 (Amino Acid Synthesis - Undeclared): 'phenylalanine oxygenase reduces phenylalanine to produce the tyrosine' (tyrosine is the product)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "tyrosine is the product of PAH; loss of PAH activity lowers tyrosine production, so product co-varies with enzyme activity (LoF => Tyr falls)."
    .
