    ; pmo:mechanism "accumulated homocysteine is salvaged by remethylation (methionine synthase / betaine-homocysteine methyltransferase) back to methionine; higher homocysteine drives higher methionine remethylation flux, so plasma methionine rises (the characteristic high-methionine signature of CBS deficiency)."
