    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "PMID 27722792; (Metabolic Brain Disease; abstract/conclusion (Saha et al., Decreased sensitivity of palmitoyl protein thioesterase 1-deficient neurons to chemical anoxia)); “Altogether, our results indicate that PPT1 deficiency in neurons causes functional changes in complexes I and IV of the mitochondrial electron transport chain.” | Genetic loss of PPT1 (do(PPT1=0) in Ppt1-/- neurons) causally changes mitochondrial complex IV (cytochrome c oxidase) function, linking the NCL enzyme island member ppt1_activity to the core node mitochondrial_complex_iv_activity; direction unresolved so sign=?. [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "PPT1 (CLN1) is a lysosomal/cytosolic palmitoyl-protein thioesterase whose loss (Ppt1-/- = natural do()) alters depalmitoylation/turnover of mitochondrial proteins (PPT1 associates with the F1 complex of ATP synthase), producing functional changes in mitochondrial electron-transport-chain complexes I and IV; net direction on complex IV activity is genuinely ambiguous from the cited source (decreased inhibitor sensitivity, not clearly reduced baseline activity), so sign = ?."
    .
