    ; dcterms:source "genetic_lof_gof do(): biallelic PRODH loss-of-function = hyperprolinemia type I (OMIM #239500), a natural human do() on the enzyme. Intervention: germline PRODH LoF; measured endpoint: ELEVATED plasma proline (chronic/lifelong), characteristically WITHOUT urinary delta-1-pyrroline-5-carboxylate excretion (distinguishes type I from P5CDH/type II); context: human, systemic plasma. do(PRODH up) => plasma proline down (sign -). Mitsubuchi H et al., biochemical and clinical features of hereditary hyperprolinemia (PMC4282441). Sign-concordant with sibling p5c_dehydrogenase_activity -(-)-> plasma_proline in this fragment."
    ; pmo:mechanism "PRODH (proline dehydrogenase/oxidase) catalyzes the first committed step of proline catabolism (L-proline -> delta-1-pyrroline-5-carboxylate) in mitochondria; biallelic PRODH loss-of-function backs up the proline pool systemically, so enzyme activity up lowers plasma proline"
    .
