<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Ahydroxyacyl_coa_dehydrogenase_activity%3Anegative%3Aglutamate_dehydrogenase_activity> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hydroxyacyl_coa_dehydrogenase_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/glutamate_dehydrogenase_activity> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "genetic_lof_gof do(): HADH/SCHAD loss-of-function = SCHAD hyperinsulinism (HADH deficiency), a natural human do() on the enzyme. Intervention: germline HADH LoF; measured endpoint: disinhibited / increased GDH activity -> leucine/protein-sensitive hyperinsulinaemic hypoglycaemia; context: human pancreatic beta-cell / hepatocyte, chronic Mendelian. do(HADH up) => GDH activity down (sign -). PMID:20670938 (Filling C, Stanley CA et al., J Biol Chem 2010 — direct SCHAD-GDH inhibitory protein-protein interaction, the primary mechanistic proof); DOI:10.1172/JCI11294 (Clayton PT et al., J Clin Invest 2001;108:457-465); Orphanet J Rare Dis 2021, DOI:10.1186/s13023-021-02088-6 (PMC8567654, GDH-disinhibition mechanism). Lands into the existing glutamate_dehydrogenase_activity -(+)-> beta_cell_insulin_secretion axis; replaces the held CB-MET-002 (confounded HADH->hepatic_ketogenesis)."
    ; pmo:mechanism "HADH (short-chain 3-hydroxyacyl-CoA dehydrogenase) protein moonlights as a direct inhibitor of glutamate dehydrogenase (GLUD1) in the pancreatic beta cell; loss of HADH releases GDH from inhibition, raising GDH activity, glutamate-driven anaplerosis and insulin secretion, so HADH activity up lowers GDH activity"
    .
