    ; dcterms:source "OMIM #277900 Wilson disease (raised free/non-ceruloplasmin serum copper); Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine (Wilson disease: low total but high free serum copper, hepatic copper accumulation); Boron & Boulpaep Medical Physiology (hepatobiliary copper excretion)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "hepatobiliary excretion is the major route of copper elimination; when biliary copper efflux fails (ATP7B LoF, Wilson disease), copper accumulates in the liver and spills into plasma as the loosely-bound non-ceruloplasmin (\"free\") fraction, so lower hepatic copper excretion raises free serum copper"
    .
