    ; pmo:causalEvidence "perturbation"
    ; dcterms:source "Boron & Boulpaep Medical Physiology (IL-6 endogenous pyrogen -> fever); Janeway's Immunobiology (acute-phase fever) | perturbation (bidirectional): IL-6-deficient mice fail to develop fever to LPS or IL-1beta, and intracerebroventricular recombinant IL-6 restores the fever response (opened PMC2192408) — loss and rescue of IL-6 change core temperature in the asserted direction | textbook corroboration: OpenStax Biology 2e §bio-33.3 (Homeostasis): endogenous pyrogens released by leukocytes destroying bacteria reset the hypothalamic thermostat, causing fever — corroborates IL-6 as endogenous pyrogen raising core temperature.; OpenStax Biology 2e §bio-42.1 (42.1: Innate Immune Response): 'Cytokines also increase the core body temperature, causing a fever' — IL-6 is the principal circulating endogenous pyrogen."
    ; pmo:mechanism "IL-6 is the principal circulating endogenous pyrogen reaching the OVLT/hypothalamus -> PGE2 -> fever"
    .
