    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "StatPearls NBK493179 (Biochemistry, Ketogenesis): ketogenesis is stimulated by counter-regulatory hormones including glucagon. Lehninger 7th ed. ch.17 & ch.23 (glucagon promotes ketogenesis in fasting/diabetes)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "glucagon disinhibits CPT-1 (malonyl-CoA falls) and increases FFA supply, raising hepatic beta-oxidation and ketogenic flux (permissive with low insulin)"
    .
