    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger 7th ed. ch.17 & ch.23 (insulin deficiency -> diabetic ketoacidosis); Boron & Boulpaep 3rd ed. ch.58 | textbook corroboration: OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-145 (25.2: Physical Characteristics of Urine): 'without the action of insulin, the cells cannot take up [glucose], so...cells are forced to use fat as their energy source, and fat consumed at such a level produces excessive ketones as byproducts' — corroborates insulin suppression of ketogenesis."
    ; pmo:mechanism "insulin (via raised malonyl-CoA, inhibited CPT-1) suppresses hepatic ketogenesis"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepcidin> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/ferroportin_activity> .
