    ; pmo:causalEvidence "perturbation"
    ; dcterms:source "Nemeth et al. 2004 Science 306:2090 (PMID 15514116); Parmar2019 BioModels MODEL1805140003 (PMID 30608934); Ganz & Nemeth 2012 BBA review | textbook corroboration: OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-098 (17.11: Organs with Secondary Endocrine Functions): 'Hepcidins block the release of iron from cells in the body, helping to regulate iron homeostasis'; OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-137 (23.8: Chemical Digestion and Absorption - A Closer Look): 'When the body needs iron...there is increased uptake of iron from the intestine and accelerated release of iron into the bloodstream' — low body iron reduces hepcidin, releasing ferroportin-mediated export (implied mechanism) [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "hepcidin binds ferroportin on enterocytes/macrophages/hepatocytes, triggering its internalization and degradation, lowering cellular iron export"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/ferroportin_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_iron> .
