    ; pmo:mechanism "high hepatic iron stores increase BMP6 expression and BMP-SMAD signaling, raising hepcidin transcription (stores-regulator of hepcidin)"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepcidin> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/ferritin_stores> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Ahepcidin%3Apositive%3Aferritin_stores> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepcidin> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/ferritin_stores> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "mechanistic_model"
    ; dcterms:source "Nemeth et al. 2004 Science 306:2090 (PMID 15514116); Masison2022 BioModels MODEL2211030002 (doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0281401) [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "by degrading ferroportin, hepcidin traps iron inside macrophages and hepatocytes, increasing intracellular ferritin-bound iron stores"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/erythropoietic_iron_demand> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepcidin> .
