<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aaco2_activity%3Apositive%3Aurinary_aconitic_acid> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/aco2_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/urinary_aconitic_acid> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Plasma metabolomics in ACO2 deficiency (PMID 28463998, Schwarzmayr et al. 2017): cis-aconitate and isocitrate markedly decreased in ACO2-deficient patients; Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry Ch. 16 (aconitase reaction: citrate -> cis-aconitate -> isocitrate) | intervention: do(ACO2 loss-of-function) [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "ACO2 converts citrate to cis-aconitate (intermediate) and then to isocitrate; ACO2 deficiency causes cis-aconitate to FALL (net: less aconitate produced from the accumulating citrate at physiological equilibrium). Higher ACO2 activity produces more cis-aconitate from citrate. PMID 28463998 confirms cis-aconitate is reduced 36.9-fold in ACO2-deficient plasma."
    .
