    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Alpha-ketoglutarate dehydrogenase deficiency (OMIM 203740; Orphanet oxoglutaric aciduria): elevated urine alpha-ketoglutarate is the hallmark biomarker; MedLink Neurology (alpha-KG dehydrogenase deficiency review); Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry Ch. 16 (TCA cycle: OGDH complex, step 4) | intervention: do(OGDH / alpha-ketoglutarate dehydrogenase complex deficiency)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "The alpha-ketoglutarate (2-oxoglutarate) dehydrogenase complex (OGDH) oxidatively decarboxylates alpha-ketoglutarate to succinyl-CoA in the TCA cycle; reduced OGDH activity leaves alpha-ketoglutarate unconsumed, causing it to accumulate and spill into urine — do(OGDH deficiency) => elevated urinary alpha-ketoglutarate"
    .
