    ; dcterms:source "Fumarase deficiency / fumaric aciduria (FH; OMIM 606812): urinary fumarate, succinate, and citrate elevated; fumarate hydratase activity profoundly decreased in fibroblasts (PMID 10805328, Kerrigan et al. 2000 Ann Neurol); Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry Ch. 16 (fumarase, TCA step 7: fumarate -> malate) | intervention: do(FH / fumarate hydratase deficiency) [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Fumarate hydratase (fumarase, FH) catalyses the reversible hydration of fumarate to malate in the TCA cycle; FH deficiency blocks fumarate consumption, causing fumarate accumulation in plasma — do(FH deficiency) => plasma fumarate UP"
