    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "SCOT/OXCT1 deficiency (OMIM 245050): persistent non-fasting ketosis; elevated beta-hydroxybutyric acid and acetoacetic acid detected in urine (ScienceDirect clinical case series, OMIM 245050 entry); Scriver's OMMBID (SCOT deficiency: ketoaciduria) | intervention: do(SCOT / OXCT1 loss-of-function)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "SCOT (succinyl-CoA:3-oxoacid CoA transferase, OXCT1) activates acetoacetate to acetoacetyl-CoA for peripheral ketolysis; SCOT deficiency blocks ketone body utilisation, causing ketone bodies including 3-hydroxybutyrate to accumulate in blood and spill into urine — reduced SCOT raises urinary 3-hydroxybutyrate"
    .
