    ; pmo:mechanism "SCOT deficiency blocks peripheral ketolysis; 3-hydroxybutyrate (the predominant circulating ketone body at steady state) accumulates in plasma — reduced SCOT raises plasma hydroxybutyrate (generic hydroxybutyrate node, same CHEBI:20067 as plasma_3_hydroxybutyrate)"
    .
