    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Primary hyperoxaluria type 1 (AGXT; OMIM 259900): plasma oxalate elevation leading to systemic oxalosis documented in PH1 (Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine; Scriver's OMMBID — PH1: hyperoxaluria, nephrolithiasis, systemic oxalosis with elevated plasma oxalate) | intervention: do(AGT / AGXT loss-of-function)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "AGT (alanine-glyoxylate aminotransferase) detoxifies glyoxylate to glycine; AGT deficiency (PH1) leads to glyoxylate overproduction of oxalate by LDH; as renal function declines from oxalate nephropathy, plasma oxalate accumulates (systemic oxalosis) — reduced AGT raises plasma oxalate"
    .
