    ; dcterms:source "Primary hyperoxaluria type 1 (AGXT; OMIM 259900): diagnostic signature is elevated urinary oxalate AND glycolate (Scriver's OMMBID — PH1: 'hyperoxaluria with elevated urinary glycolate + oxalate is the diagnostic signature'); elevated plasma glycolate in systemic PH1 | intervention: do(AGT / AGXT loss-of-function)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "In AGT deficiency (PH1), undegraded glyoxylate is reduced by lactate dehydrogenase to glycolate; elevated plasma glycolate is part of the diagnostic signature — reduced AGT activity raises plasma glycolate"
