    ; dcterms:source "Primary hyperoxaluria type 1 (AGXT; OMIM 259900): glyoxylate accumulation is the proximate metabolic event (Scriver's OMMBID / Saudubray, Inborn Metabolic Diseases — PH1: glyoxylate accumulates and is diverted to oxalate and glycolate); Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (glyoxylate metabolism) | intervention: do(AGT / AGXT loss-of-function)"
