    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Primary hyperoxaluria type 2 (GRHPR; OMIM 260000): hyperoxaluria with elevated plasma oxalate in advanced disease (Scriver's OMMBID — PH2: hyperoxaluria and systemic oxalosis) | intervention: do(GRHPR loss-of-function)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "GRHPR (glyoxylate reductase / hydroxypyruvate reductase) reduces glyoxylate to glycolate (detoxification); GRHPR deficiency (PH2) diverts glyoxylate to oxalate via LDH, causing oxalate overproduction — reduced GRHPR raises plasma oxalate (systemic oxalosis as GFR falls)"
