    ; pmo:mechanism "Mevalonate kinase (MVK) phosphorylates mevalonate to 5-phosphomevalonate in the isoprenoid/cholesterol biosynthesis pathway; deficiency causes mevalonate to accumulate and be excreted in urine (mevalonic aciduria) — reduced MVK activity raises urinary mevalonate"
