    ; dcterms:source "Scriver et al., OMMBID — phenylketonuria (PAH, OMIM 261600): musty-odour urine reflects phenylpyruvate excretion; Saudubray, Inborn Metabolic Diseases (PKU, classic marker urinary phenylpyruvate); Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry Ch. 18 (phenylalanine/tyrosine catabolism) | intervention: Phenylketonuria (PAH loss-of-function, OMIM 261600)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Phenylalanine hydroxylase (PAH) converts phenylalanine to tyrosine; PAH deficiency causes phenylalanine accumulation that overflows into the transaminase pathway producing phenylpyruvate (a phenylketone), excreted in urine — reduced PAH activity raises urinary phenylpyruvate"
    .
