    ; pmo:mechanism "Elevated phenylalanine (e.g., in PKU) is transaminated to phenylpyruvate, which can be reduced or oxidized via minor shunt pathways to phenyllactic acid and mandelic acid; elevated plasma phenylalanine drives increased flux through these alternative catabolic routes, raising urinary mandelic acid"
    .
