    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "PKU (PAH deficiency, OMIM 261600): phenylacetylglutamine excretion is elevated in untreated PKU patients and correlates with circulating phenylalanine levels — Blau et al., Physician's Guide to Inherited Metabolic Diseases; Saudubray, Inborn Metabolic Diseases | intervention: PAH deficiency (phenylketonuria) raising plasma phenylalanine [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Elevated phenylalanine (in PKU) is transaminated to phenylpyruvate and then oxidatively decarboxylated to phenylacetate; phenylacetate is conjugated with glutamine in the liver by glutamine N-phenylacetyltransferase to form phenylacetylglutamine (PAG), which is excreted in urine — elevated plasma phenylalanine drives more PAG formation"
    .
