    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Canavan disease (ASPA deficiency, OMIM 271900): pathognomonic massive N-acetylaspartic aciduria — Saudubray, Inborn Metabolic Diseases; Scriver's OMMBID (Canavan disease: NAA acidemia and NAA aciduria are the diagnostic hallmarks); Blau, Physician's Guide to Inherited Metabolic Diseases | intervention: ASPA loss-of-function (Canavan disease)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Aspartoacylase (ASPA) hydrolyzes N-acetyl-L-aspartate (NAA) to aspartate and acetate in the brain; ASPA deficiency (Canavan disease) prevents NAA catabolism in oligodendrocytes, causing NAA to overflow into blood and urine — reduced ASPA activity raises urinary NAA up to 60-fold above normal"
    .
