    ; dcterms:source "Canavan disease (ASPA deficiency, OMIM 271900): NAA is elevated in plasma (NAA acidemia) as well as urine — Saudubray, Inborn Metabolic Diseases; Scriver's OMMBID | intervention: ASPA loss-of-function (Canavan disease)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "ASPA deficiency prevents brain NAA catabolism; excess NAA passes from the CNS extracellular fluid to blood, elevating plasma NAA — reduced ASPA activity raises plasma N-acetylaspartate"
    .
