    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "5-Oxoprolinase deficiency (OPLAH, OMIM 260005): 5-oxoprolinuria; also glutathione synthetase deficiency (OMIM 266130) causes 5-oxoprolinuria by the same cycle — Saudubray, Inborn Metabolic Diseases; Scriver's OMMBID (gamma-glutamyl cycle disorders) | intervention: OPLAH loss-of-function (5-oxoprolinase deficiency)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "5-Oxoprolinase (OPLAH) hydrolyzes 5-oxoproline (pyroglutamic acid) to L-glutamate in the gamma-glutamyl cycle; OPLAH deficiency allows 5-oxoproline to accumulate and be excreted in urine (5-oxoprolinuria / pyroglutamic aciduria) — reduced oxoprolinase activity raises urinary pyroglutamate"
    .
