    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Hereditary tyrosinemia type 1 (FAH deficiency, OMIM 276700): elevated urinary succinylacetone on organic-acid GC-MS is the diagnostic hallmark — Saudubray, Inborn Metabolic Diseases; Scriver's OMMBID; Blau, Physician's Guide | intervention: FAH loss-of-function (hereditary tyrosinemia type 1)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "FAH deficiency diverts fumarylacetoacetate to succinylacetone, which is filtered and excreted in urine; reduced FAH activity raises urinary succinylacetone — the most reliable diagnostic marker for tyrosinemia type 1 on urine organic acid analysis"
    .
