    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "MMSDH deficiency (ALDH6A1, OMIM 614105): 3-hydroxyisobutyrate aciduria is the reported urinary metabolite signature — Sass et al., J Inherit Metab Dis 2012 (PMID 21863277: '3-hydroxyisobutyrate aciduria and mutations in the ALDH6A1 gene'); Saudubray, Inborn Metabolic Diseases | intervention: ALDH6A1 loss-of-function (MMSDH deficiency) [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Methylmalonate semialdehyde dehydrogenase (MMSDH/ALDH6A1) oxidizes methylmalonate semialdehyde (MMSA) to propionyl-CoA in valine and thymine catabolism; MMSDH deficiency blocks MMSA oxidation, causing it to be reduced back to 3-hydroxyisobutyrate (via HIBADH running in reverse), resulting in 3-hydroxyisobutyrate aciduria — reduced MMSDH activity raises urinary 3-hydroxyisobutyrate"
    .
