    ; dcterms:source "Harrison's PIM, The Porphyrias (PCT: elevated urinary porphyrins); StatPearls NBK563209; ASH Education Program 2024 (PCT: urine and plasma porphyrins elevated, predominantly uroporphyrin). | intervention: UROD loss-of-function (porphyria cutanea tarda, OMIM 176100)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "UROD deficiency (PCT) causes massive urinary excretion of total porphyrins (uroporphyrin, heptacarboxylporphyrin, hexacarboxyl- and pentacarboxylporphyrin intermediates). do(UROD_activity down) → urinary total porphyrin rises."
    .
