<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Acoproporphyrinogen_oxidase_activity%3Anegative%3Aurinary_coproporphyrin> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/coproporphyrinogen_oxidase_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/urinary_coproporphyrin> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Harrison's PIM, The Porphyrias (HCP: CPOX deficiency, elevated urinary coproporphyrin III); OMIM 121300 (hereditary coproporphyria); OMIM 612732 (CPOX gene). CPOX activity ~50% in heterozygotes; urinary coproporphyrin III greatly elevated. | intervention: CPOX loss-of-function (hereditary coproporphyria, OMIM 121300)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "CPOX (coproporphyrinogen III oxidase) catalyses step 6 of heme synthesis (coproporphyrinogen III → protoporphyrinogen IX). Deficiency (hereditary coproporphyria, HCP) causes massive accumulation of coproporphyrinogen III, which is oxidised to coproporphyrin III and excreted in urine."
    .
