    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "PCT: elevated urinary pentacarboxylporphyrin as an intermediate of the UROD-blocked decarboxylation cascade. StatPearls NBK563209; ScienceDirect: ‘porphyria cutanea tarda: accumulation of hexacarboxylic porphyrinogen and pentacarboxylic porphyrinogen’ (PCR: uro, hepta, hexa, pentacarboxyl porphyrins). Harrison's PIM, The Porphyrias. | intervention: UROD loss-of-function (porphyria cutanea tarda, OMIM 176100)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "UROD sequentially decarboxylates the 8-carboxyl uroporphyrinogen III through 7-, 6-, 5-carboxyl intermediates to 4-carboxyl coproporphyrinogen. Deficiency (PCT) causes accumulation of all intermediates including pentacarboxylporphyrin (5-COOH), which appears in urine."
    .
