    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Harrison's PIM, The Porphyrias (EPP: FECH deficiency, elevated erythrocyte free protoporphyrin); OMIM 177000 (EPP1, FECH LoF); Orphanet J Rare Dis 2009 (EPP: erythrocyte PPIX markedly elevated). | intervention: Ferrochelatase (FECH) loss-of-function (erythropoietic protoporphyria, OMIM 177000)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Ferrochelatase (FECH) inserts Fe2+ into protoporphyrin IX to form heme (last step of heme biosynthesis). Deficiency (erythropoietic protoporphyria, EPP) causes protoporphyrin IX to accumulate in erythrocytes, rising to pathologically elevated concentrations."
