    ; dcterms:source "Harrison's PIM, The Porphyrias (EPP: elevated erythrocyte free protoporphyrin); OMIM 177000 (EPP1: erythrocyte free PPIX elevated). Lehninger, heme biosynthesis (ferrochelatase = terminal step). | intervention: Ferrochelatase (FECH) loss-of-function (erythropoietic protoporphyria, OMIM 177000)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Ferrochelatase deficiency (EPP) is the canonical cause of elevated erythrocyte free (non-zinc-chelated) protoporphyrin. Free protoporphyrin IX accumulates because the terminal heme-synthesis step is blocked. do(ferrochelatase_activity down) → erythrocyte free porphyrin rises."
