    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "American Porphyria Foundation, HCP: ‘markedly elevated fecal coproporphyrin’ is characteristic of HCP; OMIM 121300; Harrison's PIM, The Porphyrias (HCP: elevated fecal and urinary coproporphyrin III). | intervention: CPOX loss-of-function (hereditary coproporphyria, OMIM 121300)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "CPOX deficiency (hereditary coproporphyria, HCP) causes accumulation of coproporphyrin III that is excreted into bile and hence appears at markedly elevated concentrations in feces. Fecal coproporphyrin is a key diagnostic marker of HCP."
