    ; dcterms:source "Harrison's PIM, The Porphyrias (EPP: elevated fecal protoporphyrin); OMIM 177000 (EPP1); GeneReviews: ‘elevated free protoporphyrin in feces’ in erythropoietic protoporphyria. | intervention: Ferrochelatase (FECH) loss-of-function (erythropoietic protoporphyria, OMIM 177000)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Ferrochelatase deficiency (EPP) leads to accumulation of protoporphyrin IX in the liver and biliary tree; excess protoporphyrin is excreted into bile and appears in feces at elevated levels. Fecal protoporphyrin is elevated in EPP."
