    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "MedScape 'Sulfite Oxidase Deficiency and Molybdenum Cofactor Deficiency': elevated thiosulfate in plasma and urine; GeneReviews NBK575630 (MoCD): ‘accumulation of sulfite, taurine, S-sulfocysteine and thiosulfate’. Same mechanism as the existing sulfite_oxidase_activity → urinary_thiosulfate edge; plasma compartment parallels urine. | intervention: Sulfite oxidase (SUOX) or molybdenum cofactor loss-of-function (OMIM 272300 / 252150)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "When sulfite oxidase (SUOX) or molybdenum cofactor is deficient, excess sulfite accumulates and is converted to thiosulfate (a minor alternative disposal pathway), raising both urinary and plasma thiosulfate. do(sulfite_oxidase_activity down) → plasma thiosulfate rises."
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/cox_1_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_thromboxane_b2> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Acox_1_activity%3Apositive%3Aplasma_thromboxane_b2> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/cox_1_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_thromboxane_b2> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "Frontiers Pharmacology 2019 (measurement of thromboxane biosynthesis): TXB2 is the stable degradation product of platelet COX-1-derived TXA2; aspirin reduces urinary and plasma TXB2. Circ Res 2006 (de novo COX-1 synthesis counteracts aspirin). Lehninger, arachidonic acid cascade. | intervention: Aspirin (irreversible COX-1 inhibition) reduces plasma TXB2; COX-1 LoF (rare OMIM 601539) also reduces TXB2"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Platelet COX-1 (PTGS1) converts arachidonic acid to PGH2, which is then converted by thromboxane synthase to TXA2; TXA2 spontaneously hydrolyses to stable TXB2 (the measured plasma analyte). Aspirin irreversibly acetylates COX-1 in platelets, reducing TXB2 synthesis. do(COX-1 activity down) → plasma TXB2 falls."
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/alox12_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_12_hete> .
