    ; dcterms:source "ALOX12 Wikipedia; ScienceDirect 'Arachidonate 12 Lipoxygenase': platelets express high ALOX12 levels and generate 12S-HETE from arachidonic acid. (ALOX12 mutation in bleeding diathesis). Lehninger, lipoxygenase pathway of arachidonate metabolism. | intervention: ALOX12 loss-of-function (OMIM not established for isolated deficiency; pharmacological: ALOX12 inhibitor reduces plasma 12-HETE) [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "ALOX12 (platelet-type 12S-lipoxygenase) converts arachidonic acid to 12(S)-HETE in platelets and other cells. Greater ALOX12 activity produces more 12-HETE, which is released into plasma. Conversely, ALOX12 LoF reduces plasma 12-HETE."
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/paf_acetylhydrolase_activity> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_paf> .
