    ; dcterms:source "PMC507371 (PAF-AH deficiency missense mutation near active site); PMC2674695 (emerging roles of PAF acetylhydrolase): PAF-AH LoF → elevated plasma PAF → asthma/inflammatory risk. PMID:12547653 (plasma PAF-AH and elevated PAF in deficiency states). | intervention: PAF-AH (PLA2G7) loss-of-function (PAF-AH deficiency; V279F, common Japanese variant) [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "PAF acetylhydrolase (PAF-AH / PLA2G7) degrades platelet-activating factor by hydrolysing the sn-2 acetyl ester, inactivating PAF. Deficiency (autosomal recessive PAF-AH deficiency, common in East Asia: V279F mutation) impairs PAF catabolism, raising plasma PAF levels."
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/glucocerebrosidase_activity> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_glucosylsphingosine> .
