    ; dcterms:source "Am J Hematol 2017 (PMID on PMC5234703): ‘Glucosylsphingosine is a key biomarker of Gaucher disease’; plasma lyso-Gb1 in GD patients 180 ng/ml vs 1.5 ng/ml healthy controls. Int J Mol Sci 2021 (PMC12940242): glucosylsphingosine (lyso-Gb1) reliable GD biomarker. OMIM 230800 (GBA LoF, Gaucher disease). | intervention: GBA (glucocerebrosidase) loss-of-function (Gaucher disease, OMIM 230800)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Glucocerebrosidase (GBA/acid beta-glucosidase) cleaves glucosylceramide to ceramide + glucose; it also processes glucosylsphingosine (lyso-Gb1/lyso-GL1). Deficiency (Gaucher disease, GD) causes massive lysosomal accumulation of glucosylceramide and its deacylated lysolipid glucosylsphingosine, which rises in plasma to >100× normal."
    .
