    ; pmo:mechanism "HSD3B7 (3beta-hydroxy-Delta5-C27-steroid oxidoreductase) catalyzes the second step of bile acid synthesis; deficiency (congenital bile acid synthesis defect type 1, OMIM 607765) abolishes normal primary bile acid synthesis, but causes accumulation of atypical sulfated bile alcohols and unusual bile acids that are excreted in urine. Net urinary total bile acid direction is ambiguous: normal primary bile acids fall but atypical forms rise."
