<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Asardh_activity%3Anegative%3Aurinary_sarcosine> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/sardh_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/urinary_sarcosine> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Sarcosinemia OMIM 268900; GARD disease page: sarcosinemia characterized by elevated sarcosine in blood AND urine (sarcosinuria); overflow mechanism identical to other aminoacidurias. | intervention: do(SARDH loss-of-function) — sarcosinemia OMIM 268900"
    ; pmo:mechanism "SARDH deficiency causes sarcosine to accumulate in plasma; elevated plasma sarcosine exceeds renal reabsorption capacity (overflow aminoaciduria), resulting in sarcosinuria. do(SARDH LoF) -> plasma sarcosine up -> urinary sarcosine rises."
    .
