    ; dcterms:source "Hyperargininemia (argininemia) OMIM 207800; ARG1 gene; MedLink Neurology — elevated CSF arginine is documented in all ARG1-deficient patients; Lehninger, urea cycle (arginase step 5, arginine -> ornithine + urea). | intervention: do(ARG1 loss-of-function) — hyperargininemia/argininemia OMIM 207800"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Arginase (ARG1) hydrolyzes arginine to ornithine + urea; arginine is the substrate. ARG1 deficiency (hyperargininemia) causes arginine to accumulate in plasma and CSF. MedLink Neurology confirms 'increased concentration of arginine is found in the plasma and CSF of all affected individuals' with arginase deficiency."
