    ; pmo:mechanism "SLC6A19 (B0AT1) is the apical sodium-dependent neutral amino acid transporter in renal proximal tubule and intestine. LoF (Hartnup disease) causes failure to reabsorb neutral amino acids from glomerular filtrate, resulting in massive neutral aminoaciduria (elevated total urinary amino acids). do(SLC6A19 LoF) -> urinary total amino acid excretion rises."
    .
