    ; dcterms:source "Isolated sulfite oxidase deficiency OMIM 272300; Wiley JIMD 2024 consensus guidelines (Schwahn et al.): 'elevated levels of plasma and urinary S-sulfocysteine' in SUOX/MoCo deficiency; PMC3509921 (HPLC method for S-sulfocysteine): 'increased 5–50 fold in isolated sulfite oxidase deficiency with no overlap between healthy and affected individuals'; Lehninger (cysteine catabolism, sulfite as intermediate). | intervention: do(SUOX loss-of-function) — isolated sulfite oxidase deficiency OMIM 272300"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Sulfite oxidase (SUOX) oxidizes sulfite -> sulfate (final step of cysteine catabolism). SUOX deficiency (isolated sulfite oxidase deficiency) or molybdenum cofactor deficiency causes sulfite to accumulate; excess sulfite reacts with cysteine to form S-sulfocysteine, which is massively elevated in plasma and urine. do(SUOX LoF) -> urinary S-sulfocysteine rises 5-50-fold."
    .
