    ; dcterms:source "Glutamate formiminotransferase deficiency (formiminoglutamic aciduria) OMIM 229100; MedlinePlus FTCD gene; PMC5702579 (allelic spectrum of FTCD variants in formiminoglutamic aciduria): 'marked elevation of formiminoglutamate (FIGLU) in urine and plasma'; NIH newborn screening codes FIGLU; Lehninger (histidine catabolism, FIGLU as intermediate requiring folate). | intervention: do(FTCD loss-of-function) — glutamate formiminotransferase deficiency OMIM 229100"
    ; pmo:mechanism "FTCD (formimidoyltransferase-cyclodeaminase) catalyzes the last two steps of histidine catabolism: (1) glutamate formiminotransferase transfers formimino group from FIGLU to THF -> N-formimino-THF + glutamate; (2) cyclodeaminase converts N-formimino-THF -> 5,10-methenyl-THF + NH3. FTCD deficiency blocks FIGLU degradation; FIGLU accumulates and is massively excreted in urine. do(FTCD LoF) -> urinary FIGLU rises."
