    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Gamma-glutamyl transpeptidase deficiency OMIM (GGT1 deficiency, glutathionuria/elevated gamma-glutamyl compounds); PMC5974402 (gamma-glutamyl transpeptidase deficiency caused by large homozygous deletion in GGT1): patients have elevated urinary glutathione and gamma-glutamyl compounds; PMC1852094 (gamma-glutamyl cycle, GGT1 role in degrading gamma-glutamyl peptides); Lehninger (gamma-glutamyl cycle). | intervention: do(GGT1 loss-of-function) — gamma-glutamyl transpeptidase deficiency"
    ; pmo:mechanism "GGT1 (gamma-glutamyltransferase 1/glutathione hydrolase 1) cleaves the gamma-glutamyl group from glutathione and gamma-glutamyl amino acids. GGT1 deficiency (gamma-glutamyl transpeptidase deficiency) blocks processing of gamma-glutamyl compounds in the gamma-glutamyl cycle; gamma-glutamyl amino acids including gamma-glutamylphenylalanine accumulate and spill into urine. do(GGT1 LoF) -> urinary gamma-glutamylphenylalanine rises."
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/qprt_activity> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/urinary_quinolinate> .
