    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry, tryptophan catabolism / NAD biosynthesis (QPRT step); Majewski et al., OMIM 191670 quinolinate phosphoribosyltransferase; increased urinary quinolinate documented in QPRT-deficient states and in conditions with elevated upstream kynurenine pathway flux (Bender DA, Biochem J 1989). | intervention: QPRT LoF: quinolinate phosphoribosyltransferase activity DOWN → urinary quinolinic acid UP"
    ; pmo:mechanism "QPRT (quinolinate phosphoribosyltransferase) converts quinolinate + PRPP → nicotinic acid mononucleotide (NaMN) + pyrophosphate, the committed step of the de novo NAD synthesis branch from quinolinate. QPRT LoF blocks quinolinate consumption so quinolinate accumulates and is excreted in urine."
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/haao_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/urinary_quinolinate> .
