    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry, kynurenine pathway (3-HAO step to quinolinate); Bender DA, Biochem J 1989 (tryptophan → quinolinate via 3-HAO); OMIM 604521 HAAO gene. | intervention: HAAO activity change: do(HAAO UP) → urinary quinolinate UP; do(HAAO DOWN) → urinary quinolinate DOWN"
    ; pmo:mechanism "HAAO (3-hydroxyanthranilate 3,4-dioxygenase) converts 3-hydroxyanthranilic acid → alpha-amino-beta-carboxymuconate semialdehyde, which spontaneously cyclizes to quinolinate. More HAAO activity → more quinolinate produced; HAAO LoF blocks quinolinate synthesis so urinary quinolinate falls."
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/kynureninase_activity> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/urinary_xanthurenate> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Akynureninase_activity%3Anegative%3Aurinary_xanthurenate> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/kynureninase_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/urinary_xanthurenate> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Fukuoka S et al. 2007, J Inherit Metab Dis 30:184-188 (PMID 17334708) — xanthurenic aciduria due to KYNU mutation; OMIM 236800 hydroxykynureninuria — elevated kynurenine, 3-hydroxykynurenine, xanthurenate; Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry, kynurenine pathway. | intervention: KYNU LoF (hydroxykynureninuria / xanthurenic aciduria): kynureninase activity DOWN → 3-hydroxykynurenine → xanthurenate via KAT, urinary xanthurenate UP [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Kynureninase (KYNU) hydrolyzes 3-hydroxykynurenine → 3-hydroxyanthranilic acid + L-alanine. KYNU LoF causes 3-hydroxykynurenine to accumulate; it is then transaminated by kynurenine aminotransferases (KAT, PLP-dependent) to xanthurenic acid, which is excreted in urine. Elevated xanthurenate is diagnostic of KYNU deficiency (xanthurenic aciduria, hydroxykynureninuria)."
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/kynureninase_activity> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/urinary_kynurenine> .
