    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "OMIM 236800 hydroxykynureninuria — metabolomic analysis shows elevations in kynurenine, 3-hydroxykynurenine, xanthurenate; Fukuoka S et al. PMID 17334708; Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry, kynurenine pathway. | intervention: KYNU LoF (hydroxykynureninuria): kynureninase activity DOWN → urinary kynurenine UP [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Kynureninase (KYNU) also cleaves L-kynurenine → anthranilic acid + L-alanine (the other substrate). KYNU LoF causes both L-kynurenine and 3-hydroxykynurenine to accumulate; urinary kynurenine excretion rises."
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_tyrosine> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/urinary_n_acetyltyrosine> .
