    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Blau et al., Physician's Guide to Inherited Metabolic Diseases (PDH complex deficiency — markedly elevated CSF and plasma alanine is a hallmark; pyruvate-to-alanine transamination by ALT); Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (alanine aminotransferase, ALT; pyruvate is the alanine backbone); PDH complex deficiency OMIM 312170. | intervention: do(PDHA1 LoF) — PDH complex deficiency"
    ; pmo:mechanism "PDH complex deficiency causes pyruvate accumulation; alanine aminotransferase (ALT) transamination of pyruvate + glutamate -> alanine + alpha-ketoglutarate is driven to produce excess alanine; PDH deficiency is the canonical cause of hyperalaninemia in CSF."
    .
