    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (catecholamine biosynthesis: dopamine --DBH--> norepinephrine); DBH deficiency OMIM 223360 — undetectable norepinephrine and epinephrine in plasma/CSF, dopamine accumulation; Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine (dopamine-beta-hydroxylase deficiency). | intervention: do(DBH LoF) — dopamine-beta-hydroxylase deficiency"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Dopamine beta-hydroxylase (DBH) hydroxylates dopamine to norepinephrine in noradrenergic and adrenergic neurons; dopamine in the CNS is the direct substrate of DBH, so the CSF dopamine pool co-determines CSF norepinephrine. DBH deficiency (OMIM 223360) abolishes norepinephrine while dopamine accumulates."
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/pnmt_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/csf_epinephrine> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Apnmt_activity%3Apositive%3Acsf_epinephrine> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/pnmt_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/csf_epinephrine> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (epinephrine biosynthesis: norepinephrine --PNMT--> epinephrine); Blau et al., Physician's Guide to Inherited Metabolic Diseases (catecholamine biosynthesis pathway); Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine (adrenomedullary epinephrine synthesis via PNMT). | intervention: do(PNMT LoF) — PNMT deficiency reduces epinephrine"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Phenylethanolamine N-methyltransferase (PNMT) methylates norepinephrine to epinephrine in adrenomedullary chromaffin cells and PNMT-positive CNS neurons (C1-C3 groups); PNMT activity directly controls epinephrine synthesis; reduced PNMT results in low epinephrine in CNS/CSF."
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/csf_norepinephrine> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/csf_mhpg_aldehyde> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Acsf_norepinephrine%3Apositive%3Acsf_mhpg_aldehyde> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/csf_norepinephrine> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/csf_mhpg_aldehyde> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "mechanistic_model"
    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (catecholamine catabolism: norepinephrine -> MHPG via MAO-A and COMT); Blau et al., Physician's Guide to Inherited Metabolic Diseases (CSF MHPG-aldehyde as a norepinephrine turnover marker in catecholamine-pathway defects); Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine (catecholamine metabolism; DBH deficiency and catecholamine metabolite profiles). | intervention: do(DBH LoF) lowers norepinephrine and hence MHPG-aldehyde; pharmacological MAO-A inhibition accumulates norepinephrine and lowers MHPG-aldehyde"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Norepinephrine is catabolized in the CNS by MAO-A (oxidative deamination) and COMT (O-methylation); the sequential action yields 3-methoxy-4-hydroxyphenylglycolaldehyde (MHPG-aldehyde) as an intermediate catabolite; the CSF norepinephrine pool directly determines the production rate of MHPG-aldehyde."
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/csf_epinephrine> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/csf_metanephrine> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Acsf_epinephrine%3Apositive%3Acsf_metanephrine> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/csf_epinephrine> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/csf_metanephrine> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "mechanistic_model"
    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (catecholamine catabolism: epinephrine --COMT--> metanephrine); Blau et al., Physician's Guide to Inherited Metabolic Diseases (metanephrine as epinephrine metabolite; CSF catecholamine profiles in AADC/TH/DBH deficiencies); Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine (metanephrine as epinephrine O-methylation product). | intervention: pharmacological COMT inhibition (e.g., entacapone do()) accumulates epinephrine and reduces metanephrine"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Catechol-O-methyltransferase (COMT) O-methylates epinephrine to metanephrine; metanephrine is the direct O-methyl catabolite of epinephrine; the size of the CSF epinephrine pool drives metanephrine production."
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/csf_dihydrobiopterin> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/csf_biopterin> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Acsf_dihydrobiopterin%3Apositive%3Acsf_biopterin> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/csf_dihydrobiopterin> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/csf_biopterin> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "mechanistic_model"
    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (tetrahydrobiopterin/BH4 cycle: BH4 oxidized to q-BH2 then 7,8-BH2; QDPR reduces BH2 back to BH4); Blau et al., Physician's Guide to Inherited Metabolic Diseases (QDPR/dihydropteridine-reductase deficiency OMIM 261630 — elevated CSF biopterin and BH2, low BH4); sepiapterin-reductase deficiency: elevated BH2 and biopterin in CSF. | intervention: do(QDPR LoF) — QDPR deficiency raises BH2 which oxidizes to biopterin"
    ; pmo:mechanism "7,8-dihydrobiopterin (BH2) undergoes spontaneous or enzymatic oxidation to the fully oxidized form biopterin; in the BH4 cycle, BH2 that is not reduced back to BH4 by dihydropteridine reductase (QDPR) accumulates and oxidizes to biopterin; a larger BH2 pool yields more biopterin."
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/gch1_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/csf_neopterin> .
