    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Blau et al., Physician's Guide to Inherited Metabolic Diseases (GCH1 deficiency / Dopa-responsive dystonia: LOW CSF neopterin AND tetrahydrobiopterin — GCH1 is the rate-limiting upstream enzyme for all pterins including neopterin); GCH1 deficiency OMIM 600225; Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (GTP cyclohydrolase I: GTP -> 7,8-dihydroneopterin triphosphate). | intervention: do(GCH1 LoF) — GCH1 deficiency (Dopa-responsive dystonia): neopterin falls"
    ; pmo:mechanism "GTP cyclohydrolase I (GCH1) catalyzes the first committed step in BH4 biosynthesis, converting GTP to 7,8-dihydroneopterin triphosphate (D-NH2P); D-NH2P is the shared precursor of both BH4 and neopterin; reduced GCH1 activity (Dopa-responsive dystonia, GCH1 deficiency) lowers D-NH2P, reducing both CSF neopterin and BH4."
    .
