    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Cerebral folate deficiency (FOLR1 mutations, OMIM 613068) — severely low CSF 5-MTHF with normal blood folate is the diagnostic hallmark; Blau et al., Physician's Guide to Inherited Metabolic Diseases (cerebral folate deficiency: FOLR1 deficiency gives isolated low CSF 5-MTHF); Boron & Boulpaep Medical Physiology (choroid plexus secretion of CSF; folate transport across blood-CSF barrier). | intervention: do(FOLR1 LoF) — cerebral folate deficiency"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Folate receptor alpha (FOLR1) is expressed on the apical face of choroid plexus epithelial cells and mediates active transport of 5-methyltetrahydrofolate (5-MTHF) from blood into CSF via a receptor-mediated endocytosis/transcytosis mechanism; loss of FOLR1 function abolishes 5-MTHF transport into CSF while blood folate remains normal."
    .
