    ; dcterms:source "GABA-transaminase deficiency (ABAT, OMIM 613163) — markedly elevated CSF and plasma GABA, beta-alanine, and taurine; Blau et al., Physician's Guide to Inherited Metabolic Diseases (ABAT/GABA-T deficiency: elevated CSF beta-alanine as a substrate of ABAT); Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (GABA catabolism by GABA-T; ABAT also acts on beta-amino acids). | intervention: do(ABAT LoF) — GABA-transaminase deficiency"
    ; pmo:mechanism "4-aminobutyrate aminotransferase (ABAT/GABA-transaminase) catabolizes multiple gamma- and beta-amino acids, including GABA, beta-alanine, and taurine; beta-alanine is a direct substrate (beta-alanine + alpha-ketoglutarate -> malonate semialdehyde + glutamate); ABAT deficiency causes beta-alanine to accumulate."
    .
