    ; pmo:mechanism "Alpha-aminoadipic semialdehyde synthase (AASS, bifunctional lysine-ketoglutarate reductase/saccharopine dehydrogenase) initiates lysine catabolism; its deficiency (hyperlysinemia) abolishes lysine degradation, causing lysine to accumulate in plasma and CSF."
