    ; dcterms:source "Histidinemia (HAL/histidase deficiency, OMIM 235800) — elevated plasma and CSF histidine; Blau et al., Physician's Guide to Inherited Metabolic Diseases (histidinemia: histidine elevated in plasma, urine, and CSF); Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (histidine catabolism: HAL deaminates histidine to urocanate). | intervention: do(HAL LoF) — histidinemia"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Histidine ammonia-lyase (HAL/histidase) converts histidine to urocanate + ammonia; HAL deficiency (histidinemia) blocks histidine catabolism, causing histidine to accumulate in plasma and CSF."
