    ; dcterms:source "Tyrosinemia type III (HPD deficiency, OMIM 276710) — elevated plasma and CSF tyrosine; Blau et al., Physician's Guide to Inherited Metabolic Diseases (tyrosinemia type III: HPD deficiency causes hypertyrosinemia); Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (tyrosine catabolism: transamination to HPP, then HPD). | intervention: do(HPD LoF) — tyrosinemia type III"
    ; pmo:mechanism "4-hydroxyphenylpyruvate dioxygenase (HPD) acts downstream of tyrosine transamination in tyrosine catabolism; HPD deficiency (tyrosinemia type III) blocks the catabolic pathway, causing upstream accumulation of tyrosine (and its transamination product)."
    .
