    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Canavan disease (ASPA deficiency, OMIM 271900) — elevated CSF N-acetylaspartate and decreased CNS aspartate; Blau et al., Physician's Guide to Inherited Metabolic Diseases (Canavan disease: ASPA deficiency impairs myelin N-acetylaspartate hydrolysis; aspartate as product falls); Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (N-acetylaspartate hydrolysis by aspartoacylase yields aspartate). | intervention: do(ASPA LoF) — Canavan disease: CSF aspartate falls"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Aspartoacylase (ASPA) hydrolyzes N-acetylaspartate (NAA) to aspartate + acetate in oligodendrocytes; ASPA deficiency (Canavan disease) blocks this hydrolysis, reducing aspartate production from NAA while NAA accumulates; aspartate is the direct product of ASPA and falls when the enzyme is absent."
    .
