    ; dcterms:source "Citrullinemia type I (ASS1 deficiency, OMIM 215700) — markedly elevated plasma and CSF citrulline is the biochemical hallmark; Blau et al., Physician's Guide to Inherited Metabolic Diseases (citrullinemia: ASS1 deficiency causes severe citrulline accumulation in plasma, urine, and CSF); Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (urea cycle step 3: ASS1 condenses citrulline + aspartate -> argininosuccinate). | intervention: do(ASS1 LoF) — citrullinemia type I"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Argininosuccinate synthetase (ASS1) consumes citrulline + aspartate -> argininosuccinate in the urea cycle; ASS1 deficiency (citrullinemia type I) blocks this step, causing citrulline to accumulate markedly in plasma and CSF."
    .
