    ; dcterms:source "Gyrate atrophy of the choroid and retina (OAT deficiency, OMIM 258870) — 10-20-fold elevated plasma ornithine with CSF ornithine also elevated; Blau et al., Physician's Guide to Inherited Metabolic Diseases (hyperornithinemia from OAT deficiency: ornithine elevated in plasma and CSF); Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (ornithine aminotransferase: ornithine -> P5C, connecting urea cycle and proline synthesis). | intervention: do(OAT LoF) — gyrate atrophy"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Ornithine aminotransferase (OAT) catabolizes ornithine to pyrroline-5-carboxylate (P5C) in the mitochondria; OAT deficiency (gyrate atrophy) blocks ornithine catabolism, causing ornithine to accumulate in plasma, urine, and CSF."
