    ; pmo:mechanism "4-aminobutyrate aminotransferase (ABAT) has substrate activity toward taurine (a beta-sulfinyl amino acid structurally analogous to beta-alanine); ABAT deficiency impairs taurine catabolism in addition to GABA and beta-alanine, causing taurine to accumulate in CSF alongside GABA and beta-alanine."
