    ; pmo:mechanism "Proline dehydrogenase 1 (PRODH) is the mitochondrial enzyme that oxidizes proline to pyrroline-5-carboxylate (P5C), the first step in proline catabolism; PRODH deficiency (hyperprolinemia type I) blocks proline degradation, causing proline to accumulate in plasma and CSF."
