    ; pmo:mechanism "Sarcosine dehydrogenase (SARDH) catabolizes sarcosine (N-methylglycine) to glycine + formaldehyde in the mitochondria; SARDH deficiency (sarcosinemia) abolishes this conversion, causing sarcosine to accumulate in plasma and CSF."
