    ; pmo:mechanism "Cystinosin (CTNS) is the lysosomal cystine transporter that exports cystine (the disulfide dimer of cysteine) from lysosomes into the cytoplasm; CTNS deficiency (cystinosis) causes lysosomal cystine accumulation in virtually all cell types including CNS cells, raising free cystine in CSF."
    .
