    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Jaeken et al. (1984) Neuropediatrics 15:165–168 (GABA-transaminase deficiency: elevated GABA and homocarnosine in CSF); OMIM 613163; Blau et al., Physician's Guide to Inherited Metabolic Diseases (homocarnosine as a GABA storage/transport dipeptide in CNS). | intervention: genetic LoF of ABAT (GABA-transaminase deficiency, OMIM 613163); do(ABAT LoF) -> GABA+ -> homocarnosine+"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Homocarnosine (gamma-aminobutyryl-L-histidine) is synthesised in brain by carnosine synthase (CARNS1) from GABA and L-histidine; a larger GABA pool drives more homocarnosine synthesis. In GABA-transaminase deficiency (ABAT LoF), both GABA and homocarnosine are elevated in CSF — the excess GABA substrate pushes the CARNS1 reaction forward."
    .
