    ; pmo:mechanism "Aspartoacylase (ASPA) hydrolyses N-acetylaspartate (NAA) to aspartate + acetate in oligodendrocytes; higher ASPA activity consumes NAA. LoF (Canavan disease) abolishes NAA catabolism, causing massive NAA accumulation in brain and CSF."
    .
