    ; pmo:mechanism "N-acetylaspartylglutamate (NAAG) is synthesised from NAA + glutamate by NAAG synthetases (RIMKLA/RIMKLB) in neurons; a larger NAA pool as substrate supports more NAAG synthesis. In Canavan disease (ASPA LoF), both NAA and NAAG are elevated in CSF and brain, consistent with substrate-supply push."
