    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "Kennedy et al. (2016) Science 352:aad3279 (verubecestat BACE1 inhibitor: dose-dependent reduction of CSF Abeta40/42 in humans); Vassar et al. (1999) Science 286:735–741 (BACE1 is the beta-secretase for APP cleavage); Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine (Alzheimer disease: Abeta production by BACE1 and gamma-secretase). | intervention: pharmacological BACE1 inhibition (verubecestat/atabecestat/lanabecestat clinical trials): do(BACE1 inhibitor) -> CSF Abeta falls"
    ; pmo:mechanism "BACE1 (beta-secretase 1) cleaves amyloid precursor protein (APP) at the beta-site to produce the C99 fragment, which gamma-secretase then cuts to release amyloid-beta peptides (Abeta); more BACE1 activity generates more Abeta. BACE1 inhibitors (verubecestat, atabecestat, lanabecestat) reduce CSF Abeta by ~50–80% in human clinical trials."
    .
