    ; pmo:mechanism "OCTN2 (SLC22A5) is the high-affinity sodium-dependent carnitine transporter responsible for intestinal carnitine absorption and renal tubular carnitine reabsorption; LoF causes urinary carnitine wasting, reducing plasma total carnitine (systemic primary carnitine deficiency, CDSP/OMIM 212140)"
    .
