<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Amcad_activity%3Anegative%3Aplasma_acylcarnitine> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/mcad_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_acylcarnitine> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine, 'Inherited disorders of fatty acid metabolism' (MCAD deficiency, OMIM 201450; elevated total acylcarnitines detected by newborn screening MS/MS); GeneReviews NBK1424 | intervention: ACADM LoF (MCAD deficiency, OMIM 201450)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "MCAD deficiency blocks medium-chain beta-oxidation, causing acyl-CoA species to be trapped as acylcarnitines and released into plasma; total plasma acylcarnitine rises as medium-chain acylcarnitines (C6-C10) accumulate (MCAD deficiency is the prototypical FAO disorder that elevates total plasma acylcarnitines)"
