    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "VLCAD deficiency (OMIM 201475): Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine 'Inherited disorders of fatty acid metabolism'; plasma acylcarnitine profile shows elevated C16:1 alongside C14:1 (Liebig et al. 2001, Pediatr Res PMID 11433098; Schuler et al. Biochem Markers FAO Diseases, MDPI 2021 doi:10.3390/jcm10214855) | intervention: loss-of-function of ACADVL gene (VLCAD deficiency, OMIM 201475) [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "VLCAD (ACADVL) catalyzes the first step of mitochondrial beta-oxidation of C14-C20 acyl-CoA esters; reduced VLCAD activity blocks oxidation of palmitoloeoyl-CoA (C16:1), which is esterified to carnitine and exported to plasma, raising plasma palmitoleoylcarnitine (C16:1-acylcarnitine)"
    .
