    ; dcterms:source "CPT-II deficiency (OMIM 255110): Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine 'Inherited disorders of fatty acid metabolism'; Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry Ch. 17 (carnitine shuttle); GeneReviews NBK1253 (CPT2 deficiency, elevated C12-C18 acylcarnitines including C18) | intervention: loss-of-function of CPT2 gene (CPT-II deficiency, OMIM 255110)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "CPT2 regenerates long-chain acyl-CoA from acylcarnitine on the matrix side of the inner mitochondrial membrane; reduced CPT2 activity prevents import of C18 acylcarnitines, backing them up into plasma (CPT-II deficiency raises all long-chain acylcarnitines including the C18 class)"
    .
