    ; dcterms:source "CPT-II deficiency (OMIM 255110): GeneReviews NBK1253; Schuler et al. 'Biochemical Markers for the Diagnosis of Mitochondrial Fatty Acid Oxidation Diseases' MDPI J Clin Med 2021 (C18 acylcarnitine elevated in CPT2/CACT deficiency) | intervention: loss-of-function of CPT2 gene (CPT-II deficiency, OMIM 255110)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "CPT2 cleaves C18 stearoylcarnitine to regenerate stearoyl-CoA inside mitochondria; reduced CPT2 activity strands stearoylcarnitine (C18) in the cytosol and plasma (CPT-II deficiency elevates C18 stearoylcarnitine)"
    .
