    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "CPT-II deficiency (OMIM 255110): GeneReviews NBK1253 ('C12 to C18 acylcarnitines, notably C16 and C18:1, are elevated'); Schuler et al. MDPI J Clin Med 2021 (Table of diagnostic markers for LC-FAO disorders) | intervention: loss-of-function of CPT2 gene (CPT-II deficiency, OMIM 255110)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "CPT2 regenerates oleoyl-CoA (C18:1) from oleoylcarnitine inside the mitochondrial matrix; reduced CPT2 activity causes octadecenoylcarnitine (C18:1) to accumulate in plasma (CPT-II deficiency is characterized by elevated C16 and C18:1 acylcarnitines)"
    .
