    ; dcterms:source "CPT-II deficiency (OMIM 255110): GeneReviews NBK1253; Schuler et al. MDPI J Clin Med 2021 (C18:1 oleoylcarnitine diagnostic marker in CPT2/CACT deficiency) | intervention: loss-of-function of CPT2 gene (CPT-II deficiency, OMIM 255110)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "CPT2 cleaves oleoylcarnitine (C18:1, oleic acid ester of carnitine) to regenerate oleoyl-CoA and free carnitine inside the mitochondrial matrix; reduced CPT2 activity accumulates oleylcarnitine in plasma"
    .
