    ; dcterms:source "3-hydroxyacyl-CoA dehydrogenase deficiency (HADH, OMIM 231530): Kapoor et al. J Clin Invest 2009; PMC3509842 ('plasma 3-hydroxybutyrylcarnitine... invariably present'); MedlinePlus Genetics 'familial hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia caused by SCHAD deficiency' | intervention: loss-of-function of HADH gene (3-hydroxyacyl-CoA dehydrogenase deficiency, OMIM 231530) [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Mitochondrial 3-hydroxyacyl-CoA dehydrogenase (HADH, the medium/short-chain enzyme encoded by the HADH gene) oxidizes 3-hydroxybutyryl-CoA (C4-OH-CoA) to acetoacetyl-CoA; reduced HADH activity causes 3-hydroxybutyryl-CoA to accumulate and be esterified to carnitine, raising plasma 3-hydroxybutyrylcarnitine (C4-OH), the principal diagnostic biomarker of HADH deficiency"
    .
