    ; dcterms:source "3-Methylcrotonyl-CoA carboxylase deficiency (MCC1D, OMIM 210200): Stadler et al. Eur J Hum Genet 2006 PMID 12872837 ('C5-OH acylcarnitine is the characteristic metabolite'); PMC11525625 (newborn screening outcomes with elevated 3-hydroxyisovalerylcarnitine); Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry, leucine catabolism | intervention: loss-of-function of MCCC1 gene (3-MCC deficiency type I, OMIM 210200) [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "3-Methylcrotonyl-CoA carboxylase (MCC, encoded by MCCC1/MCCC2) carboxylates 3-methylcrotonyl-CoA in leucine catabolism; reduced MCC activity causes 3-methylcrotonyl-CoA to accumulate, which is hydrated to 3-hydroxyisovaleryl-CoA and esterified to carnitine, raising plasma 3-hydroxyisovalerylcarnitine (C5-OH), the hallmark biomarker of 3-MCC deficiency on newborn screening"
    .
