    ; dcterms:source "Long-chain 3-hydroxyacyl-CoA dehydrogenase / MTP deficiency, OMIM:609016 — LoF causes accumulation of C16-OH and other long-chain 3-hydroxyacylcarnitines (primary NBS marker)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "RHEA:31159 (EC 1.1.1.211): (3S)-hydroxyhexadecanoyl-CoA + NAD(+) = 3-oxohexadecanoyl-CoA + NADH + H(+); (3S)-3-hydroxyhexadecanoyl-CoA is the substrate of the LCHAD dehydrogenase step; its carnitine ester (3-OH-C16-acylcarnitine) accumulates in plasma when flux is blocked"
    .
