    ; dcterms:source "LCHAD/MTP deficiency (OMIM 609016): Frontiers Pediatrics 2021 PMC8017228 ('eight analytes including C16:1-OH used in screening'); Orphanet ORPHA:5; Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine | intervention: loss-of-function of HADHA gene (LCHAD/MTP deficiency, OMIM 609016)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "LCHAD (HADHA subunit of MTP) oxidizes long-chain 3-hydroxyacyl-CoA substrates including 3-hydroxypalmitoleoyl-CoA (C16:1-OH-CoA); reduced activity causes 3-hydroxypalmitoleoylcarnitine (C16:1-OH) to accumulate in plasma; C16:1-OH is one of the eight diagnostic analytes used in newborn screening for LCHAD/MTP deficiency"
    .
