    ; dcterms:source "X-linked adrenoleukodystrophy (X-ALD, OMIM 300100): Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine 'Disorders of peroxisome biogenesis and metabolism'; Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry, peroxisomal beta-oxidation; plasma C26:0 is the cardinal biomarker for X-ALD diagnosis | intervention: loss-of-function of ABCD1 gene (X-linked adrenoleukodystrophy, OMIM 300100)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "ABCD1 (adrenoleukodystrophy protein, ALDP) is a peroxisomal ABC half-transporter that imports very-long-chain acyl-CoA esters (especially C24:0 and C26:0) into the peroxisome for beta-oxidation; reduced ABCD1 activity blocks import and degradation of hexacosanoic acid (C26:0), causing its elevation in plasma (the primary diagnostic marker of X-linked adrenoleukodystrophy)"
    .
