    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "X-linked adrenoleukodystrophy (X-ALD, OMIM 300100): Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine; plasma C26:0 and C24:0 (and C24:0/C22:0 ratio) are used diagnostically for X-ALD screening | intervention: loss-of-function of ABCD1 gene (X-linked adrenoleukodystrophy, OMIM 300100)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "ABCD1 imports C24:0 tetracosanoyl-CoA into the peroxisome for beta-oxidation; reduced ABCD1 activity blocks degradation of tetracosanoic acid (C24:0), elevating its plasma concentration alongside C26:0 (both C24:0 and C26:0 are diagnostic VLCFA markers in X-ALD)"
    .
