    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Glutaric aciduria type III (OMIM 231690): Knerr et al. J Inherit Metab Dis 2002 (persistent glutaric aciduria with elevated glutarylcarnitine from peroxisomal glutaryl-CoA oxidase deficiency); Gregersen et al. Pediatr Res 1991 (atypical riboflavin-responsive glutaric aciduria with deficient peroxisomal glutaryl-CoA oxidase activity); Orphanet ORPHA:35706 | intervention: loss-of-function of peroxisomal glutaryl-CoA oxidase (glutaric aciduria type III, OMIM 231690) [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Peroxisomal glutaryl-CoA oxidase catalyzes the first step of peroxisomal glutaryl-CoA oxidation; reduced activity blocks glutaryl-CoA degradation, causing it to accumulate and be esterified to carnitine, elevating plasma glutarylcarnitine (C5-DC); this is a diagnostic marker of glutaric aciduria type III"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/three_beta_hsd_delta5_desaturase_activity> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_lathosterol> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Athree_beta_hsd_delta5_desaturase_activity%3Anegative%3Aplasma_lathosterol> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/three_beta_hsd_delta5_desaturase_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_lathosterol> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Lathosterolosis (OMIM 607330): Krakowiak et al. Am J Hum Genet 2003 PMID 12189593 (novel syndrome due to deficiency of 3beta-hydroxysteroid-delta5-desaturase); PMC3897790 (plasma lathosterol elevated by GC/MS in lathosterolosis); OMIM 602286 (SC5D gene encoding sterol-C5-desaturase); Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry, cholesterol biosynthesis | intervention: loss-of-function of SC5D gene (lathosterolosis, OMIM 607330) [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "3-beta-hydroxysteroid-delta-5-desaturase (SC5D / lathosterol oxidase) catalyzes the conversion of lathosterol (5alpha-cholest-7-en-3beta-ol) to 7-dehydrocholesterol, the penultimate step in the Kandutsch-Russell cholesterol synthesis pathway; reduced SC5D activity blocks this conversion, causing lathosterol to accumulate in plasma (the diagnostic biomarker of lathosterolosis)"
    .
