    ; dcterms:source "Elevation of Circulating PSTI after Turpentine-Induced Inflammation: Hepatocytes Produce It as an Acute Phase Reactant (ScienceDirect); Release of PSTI from human hepatoblastoma cells on stimulation with cytokines (PMID:2845213); Pancreatic secretory trypsin inhibitor as an acute phase reactant (PMID:2449986); Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine (acute-phase response chapter) | intervention: do(IL-6 +) — cytokine stimulation of hepatocytes in vivo and in vitro; surgical or inflammatory stress robustly elevates plasma PSTI [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "IL-6 (and IL-1β, TNF-α) stimulate hepatocyte synthesis and secretion of SPINK1/PSTI as a positive acute-phase protein; the same mechanism operates in hepatoblastoma cells in vitro and in inflammatory models in vivo"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/prss1_acinar_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_trypsinogen> .
