    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "OMIM 176820 (KLK3/PSA): KLK3 is downregulated by castration and upregulated by testosterone; Long Terminal Repeats Act as Androgen-Responsive Enhancers for the PSA-Kallikrein Locus (Endocrinology 2012); Williams Textbook of Endocrinology (androgen-dependent prostate biology); Boron & Boulpaep Medical Physiology (sex hormone target organs); androgen deprivation therapy → PSA falls is the standard clinical intervention | intervention: do(testosterone +) — testosterone supplementation → PSA rises; androgen deprivation therapy (LHRH agonists, anti-androgens) → PSA falls; both are established clinical pharmacological perturbations"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Androgen receptor (AR) directly activates the KLK3 promoter and a ~4 kb upstream enhancer in prostate luminal epithelial cells; PSA transcription and secretion are androgen-dependent; castration (ADT) ablates PSA production while testosterone replacement restores it"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/sod3_ecm_anchoring> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_superoxide_dismutase> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Asod3_ecm_anchoring%3Anegative%3Aplasma_superoxide_dismutase> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/sod3_ecm_anchoring> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_superoxide_dismutase> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Association among extracellular superoxide dismutase genotype, plasma concentration, and comorbidity in the very old (PMC8058336, Scientific Reports 2021): SOD3 p.R231G is the most significant genetic determinant of plasma EC-SOD; Plasma EC-SOD concentration, allelic variations in SOD3 gene, and risk of MI in type 1/2 diabetes (PMC4324771, Cardiovasc Diabetol 2015): R231G at heparan sulfate binding site reduces affinity, 10-fold higher plasma SOD3; Boron & Boulpaep Medical Physiology (extracellular antioxidant systems) | intervention: do(SOD3 p.R231G, LoF for ECM-binding) — genetic variant reduces heparan sulfate binding affinity → more SOD3 released from ECM into plasma; constitutive SOD3 production unchanged, redistribution from ECM-bound to plasma pool"
    ; pmo:mechanism "SOD3/EC-SOD is anchored to heparan sulfate proteoglycans (HSPGs) in the vascular extracellular matrix via a C-terminal heparin-binding domain; the common SOD3 p.R231G variant (LoF for ECM binding) reduces affinity for HSPGs, releasing SOD3 from ECM into plasma; loss of ECM anchoring increases plasma SOD3 concentration ~10-fold"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/mmp2_fibroblast_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_mmp2> .
