    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Multicentric osteolysis nodulosis and arthropathy (MONA, OMIM 605156): all patients lacked MMP-2 gelatinolytic activity from inactivating MMP2 mutations (Nat Genet 2001; Eur J Hum Genet 2009 PMC2721823); The Complex Role of MMP-2 in Health and Disease (PMC11728377, 2025); Plasma Levels of MMP-2 and MMP-9 in Patients with Chronic Chagas Heart Disease correlated with TGF-β (PMC10132902); Regulation of MT1-MMP/MMP-2 in cardiac fibroblasts by TGF-β1 (Cardiovasc Res 2003) | intervention: do(MMP2 LoF) — inactivating mutations → absent plasma MMP-2 gelatinolytic activity (MONA disease); do(MMP2 +) → elevated plasma MMP-2 in heart failure and hypertensive heart disease (clinical observation)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "MMP-2 (72 kDa type IV collagenase/gelatinase A) is secreted by fibroblasts, osteoblasts, and vascular smooth-muscle cells; circulating plasma MMP-2 reflects the net secretion rate of tissue MMP-2; LoF mutations in MMP2 abolish gelatinolytic activity and cause multicentric osteolysis, nodulosis, and arthropathy (MONA), with absent plasma MMP-2 activity in affected patients"
    .
