    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (Nelson & Cox), purine catabolism; PNP deficiency OMIM 613179; Markert, Semin Hematol 1998 (PNP deficiency biochemistry: inosine/guanosine accumulate). | intervention: do(PNP LoF) via biallelic PNP mutations — substrate inosine accumulates"
    ; pmo:mechanism "PNP (purine nucleoside phosphorylase) phosphorolyses inosine to hypoxanthine and ribose-1-phosphate; loss of PNP blocks this step, causing inosine to accumulate in plasma (PNP deficiency: severe hypouricemia with inosine/guanosine accumulation)."
    .
