    ; dcterms:source "Rosen et al., N Engl J Med 2014 (DADA2 = ADA2 deficiency, OMIM 615688: ADA2 catalyzes adenosine -> inosine in plasma); GeneReviews DADA2 (NBK544951): ADA2 deaminates adenosine and 2'-deoxyadenosine to inosine and deoxyinosine. | intervention: do(ADA2 GoF/LoF) — ADA2 activity is the rate-limiting producer of plasma inosine from adenosine"
    ; pmo:mechanism "ADA2 (adenosine deaminase 2) deaminates extracellular adenosine to inosine in plasma; more ADA2 activity produces more plasma inosine. In DADA2 (ADA2 deficiency), inosine production from adenosine falls, and plasma adenosine rises while plasma inosine falls."
