    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (xanthine oxidoreductase, purine catabolism); Xanthinuria type I OMIM 278300 (XDH deficiency: urinary hypoxanthine and xanthine elevated, urate absent); Bosque-Jimenez et al., Int J Mol Sci 2012. | intervention: do(XDH LoF, xanthinuria type I) — hypoxanthine not oxidized, urinary hypoxanthine rises"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Xanthine oxidoreductase (XDH/XO) oxidizes hypoxanthine to xanthine (first step of purine catabolism); more XDH activity consumes hypoxanthine, lowering it. XDH deficiency (xanthinuria type I) blocks this oxidation, causing urinary hypoxanthine excretion to rise markedly."
