    ; pmo:mechanism "APRT salvages adenine (with PRPP) back to AMP; in APRT deficiency, free adenine is not salvaged and is instead oxidized by xanthine oxidase sequentially to 8-hydroxyadenine and then 2,8-dihydroxyadenine (2,8-DHA), which is insoluble and causes urolithiasis. More APRT activity = less free adenine = less 2,8-DHA produced."
    .
