    ; dcterms:source "PRPS1 superactivity OMIM 300661 (purine overproduction leading to hyperuricaemia; excess IMP pool dephosphorylated to inosine); Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (de novo purine synthesis: PRPP -> IMP -> inosine via 5'-nucleotidase); Becker & Kim, J Lab Clin Med 1987 (PRPS superactivity: overproduction of purine nucleotides). | intervention: do(PRPS1 GoF, OMIM 300661) — PRPP overproduction drives IMP accumulation; IMP dephosphorylated to plasma inosine"
    ; pmo:mechanism "PRPS1 (PRPP synthetase 1) synthesizes PRPP, the committed substrate for de novo purine biosynthesis; PRPS1 superactivity drives overproduction of the purine nucleotide pool (IMP, AMP, GMP). Excess IMP is dephosphorylated by 5'-nucleotidases to inosine, raising plasma inosine levels alongside the known downstream urate overproduction."
    .
