    ; dcterms:source "Suchi et al., Am J Hum Genet 1997; OMIM 258900 (hereditary orotic aciduria); Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry, de novo pyrimidine synthesis | intervention: UMPS LoF (OMIM 258900, hereditary orotic aciduria): biallelic UMPS mutations cause massive urinary orotic acid excretion, failure to thrive, and megaloblastic anemia [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "UMPS (UMP synthase) is a bifunctional enzyme carrying orotate phosphoribosyltransferase (OPRT) and orotidine-5'-phosphate decarboxylase (ODC) activities; it converts orotic acid -> OMP -> UMP in de novo pyrimidine biosynthesis. Loss of UMPS causes orotic acid to accumulate and be massively excreted in urine (hereditary orotic aciduria). More UMPS activity depletes the orotate substrate, lowering urinary orotate."
    .
