    ; dcterms:source "Cai et al., Cell Mol Biol Lett 2022 (PMID 36434495); OMIM 266120 (CNSHA8, congenital nonspherocytic hemolytic anemia 8); Lehninger, Nucleotide catabolism | intervention: NT5C3A LoF (OMIM 266120): biallelic NT5C3A mutations abolish erythrocyte pyrimidine 5'-nucleotidase activity, causing accumulation of high concentrations of pyrimidine nucleotides in red cells and basophilic stippling [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "NT5C3A (pyrimidine 5'-nucleotidase 1) preferentially dephosphorylates UMP and CMP in erythrocytes, removing pyrimidine nucleotides that accumulate as RNA is degraded during reticulocyte maturation. Loss of NT5C3A results in marked intracellular accumulation of pyrimidine nucleotides (UMP+CMP) in red cells, which causes ribosome aggregation and hemolytic anemia. More NT5C3A activity depletes the erythrocyte pyrimidine nucleotide pool."
    .
