    ; dcterms:source "Beutler et al., JCI 1983 (PMID 6308059); OMIM 612631 (CNSHA3, congenital nonspherocytic hemolytic anemia 3 due to AK1 deficiency); Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine, erythrocyte enzymopathies | intervention: AK1 LoF (OMIM 612631): biallelic AK1 mutations cause nonspherocytic hemolytic anemia with erythrocyte AMP accumulation secondary to impaired AMP phosphorylation [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "AK1 (adenylate kinase 1) catalyzes the reversible interconversion ATP + AMP <-> 2 ADP in erythrocytes, maintaining adenine nucleotide homeostasis. Loss of AK1 impairs conversion of AMP to ADP, causing AMP to accumulate within red cells. More AK1 activity phosphorylates AMP to ADP, reducing erythrocyte AMP concentration."
