    ; dcterms:source "Fishbein et al., Biochem Med 1978; Haller & Vissing, J Clin Invest 2004 (PMC2278656); OMIM 615511 (myopathy due to myoadenylate deaminase deficiency); Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry, purine nucleotide cycle | intervention: AMPD1 LoF (OMIM 615511): homozygous C34T (p.Q12X) abolishes muscle AMPD1 activity; forearm ischemic exercise test shows failure of plasma ammonia to rise post-exercise, used diagnostically"
    ; pmo:mechanism "AMPD1 (AMP deaminase 1, myoadenylate deaminase) deaminates AMP to IMP + NH3 in skeletal muscle as part of the purine nucleotide cycle during exercise. NH3 produced in contracting muscle enters the circulation, contributing to post-exercise rise in plasma ammonia. In AMPD1 deficiency, the post-exercise plasma ammonia rise is markedly attenuated or absent. More AMPD1 activity increases muscle ammonia production and thereby raises plasma ammonia during exercise."
