    ; pmo:mechanism "HEXB encodes the shared beta-subunit of both HexA (αβ) and HexB (ββ). HEXB deficiency eliminates both isozymes; HexA loss causes GM2 ganglioside accumulation (as in Tay-Sachs), with additional globoside (GA2) storage due to HexB loss — Sandhoff disease"
    .
