    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry Ch. 11 (lysosomal targeting via mannose-6-phosphate); I-cell disease / mucolipidosis II OMIM 252500; Scriver's Online Metabolic Bases 'I-Cell Disease and Pseudo-Hurler Polydystrophy' (Kornfeld & Sly): GNPTAB deficiency causes hypersecretion of all lysosomal hydrolases, with plasma hexosaminidase elevated 10-20x; beta-hexosaminidase is the classic serum diagnostic marker for I-cell disease | intervention: do(GNPTAB activity ↓) = I-cell disease (OMIM 252500): plasma total beta-hexosaminidase elevated 10-20-fold; leukocyte enzyme activity severely reduced"
    ; pmo:mechanism "GNPTAB (GlcNAc-1-phosphotransferase) adds the mannose-6-phosphate (M6P) targeting signal to lysosomal enzymes including beta-hexosaminidase. Without M6P, enzymes are secreted into the extracellular space instead of reaching lysosomes — I-cell disease / ML II. LoF therefore markedly elevates plasma (serum) beta-hexosaminidase."
    .
