    ; dcterms:source "Brady et al. Metabolic Bases of Inherited Disease: MPS II involves storage of both HS and DS; Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry Ch. 7 (GAG structure and catabolism) | intervention: do(IDS activity down) = Hunter syndrome / MPS II (OMIM 309900): urinary dermatan sulfate elevated along with heparan sulfate [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "IDS cleaves 2-O-sulfate from iduronate in dermatan sulfate (a GAG chain rich in iduronate-2-sulfate). When IDS is deficient (Hunter syndrome / MPS II), both heparan sulfate and dermatan sulfate accumulate and are excreted in urine."
    .
