    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry Ch. 7 (heparan sulfate catabolism); Sanfilippo D / MPS IIID OMIM 252940; Neufeld & Muenzer in Scriver's Metabolic Bases: GNS deficiency causes heparan sulfate storage — all Sanfilippo subtypes (A-D) are heparan sulfate storage diseases | intervention: do(GNS activity ↓) = Sanfilippo D / MPS IIID (OMIM 252940): heparan sulfate accumulates in lysosomes; elevated urinary HS"
    ; pmo:mechanism "GNS (N-acetylglucosamine-6-sulfatase) cleaves 6-O-sulfate from GlcNAc-6S residues in heparan sulfate. Heparan sulfate accumulates when GNS is deficient — Sanfilippo syndrome type D (MPS IIID)"
    .
