    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry Ch. 21 (ganglioside catabolism; beta-galactosidase cleaves GM1 to GM2); GM1-gangliosidosis OMIM 230500; Brunetti-Pierri & Scaglia (2008) Mol Genet Metab 94(4):391-396 (PMID 18524657): GLB1 deficiency causes GM1 storage in neurons and viscera; substrate confirmed by post-mortem and biopsy assay | intervention: do(GLB1 activity ↓) = GM1-gangliosidosis (OMIM 230500): GM1 ganglioside accumulates in neuronal lysosomes throughout CNS [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "GLB1 (lysosomal acid beta-galactosidase) cleaves terminal beta-galactose from GM1 ganglioside (yielding GM2) and from keratan sulfate/lactosylceramide. In GM1-gangliosidosis (GLB1 deficiency), GM1 ganglioside accumulates in neuronal lysosomes. Enzyme activity inversely determines tissue GM1 level."
