    ; pmo:mechanism "ARSB (arylsulfatase B / N-acetylgalactosamine-4-sulfatase) cleaves 4-O-sulfate from GalNAc-4S residues in dermatan sulfate and chondroitin-4-sulfate. Dermatan sulfate accumulates when ARSB is deficient — Maroteaux-Lamy syndrome (MPS VI)"
    .
