    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry Ch. 7 (heparan sulfate N-desulfation); Sanfilippo A / MPS IIIA OMIM 252900; Neufeld & Muenzer in Scriver's Metabolic Bases: SGSH is the first step of HS catabolism; deficiency causes heparan sulfate storage primarily in CNS neurons; urinary HS elevated | intervention: do(SGSH activity ↓) = Sanfilippo A / MPS IIIA (OMIM 252900): heparan sulfate accumulates in neuronal lysosomes; elevated urinary heparan sulfate; severe progressive neurodegeneration"
    ; pmo:mechanism "SGSH (heparan-N-sulfatase / N-sulphoglucosamine sulphohydrolase) cleaves the N-sulfate group from the non-reducing terminal glucosamine of heparan sulfate. Heparan sulfate accumulates when SGSH is deficient — Sanfilippo syndrome type A (MPS IIIA)"
    .
