<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Ahepatic_ldl_receptor_activity%3Apositive%3Ahepatocyte_cholesterol_content> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepatic_ldl_receptor_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepatocyte_cholesterol_content> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Brown & Goldstein Science 1986 (receptor-mediated LDL uptake delivers cholesterol intracellularly; LDLR is the regulated step); BioModels BIOMD0000000434 (McAuley2012) | textbook corroboration: Wong, Cells: Molecules and Mechanisms §wong-11.7 (Receptor-mediated Endocytosis - Undeclared): LDL receptor-mediated endocytosis delivers LDL to lysosome → acid hydrolases liberate free cholesterol and amino acids from lipoprotein → cholesterol delivered to hepatocyte"
    ; pmo:mechanism "hepatic LDL uptake is RECEPTOR-GATED: LDLR-mediated endocytosis -> lysosomal hydrolysis -> free cholesterol delivered to the hepatocyte regulatory pool. The rate-limiting, regulated determinant of uptake is LDLR surface activity (not plasma LDL directly): with LDLR lost (FH) the hepatocyte is cholesterol-DEPLETED despite high plasma LDL."
    .
