    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Nakatani et al., FASEB J 2009, PMID 18835926, DOI 10.1096/fj.08-114397: klotho-null mice had increased renal NaPi2a and hyperphosphatemia, and recombinant FGF23 lowered phosphate in wild-type and Fgf23-null mice but not in klotho-null or double-null mice."
    ; pmo:mechanism "alpha-klotho is the renal co-receptor that permits the FGF23-dependent reduction in NaPi-IIa/IIc-mediated phosphate reabsorption; this edge is the first-order shadow of the explicit gain modulation below"
