    ; dcterms:source "Boron & Boulpaep; Guyton & Hall: transcellular shift sets the rapid component of plasma [K+] | textbook corroboration: OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-157 (26.4: Electrolyte Balance): 'potassium passes through the cell membrane along with glucose, decreasing the amount of potassium in the blood and IF.'"
    ; pmo:mechanism "net movement of K+ from extracellular fluid into cells lowers plasma [K+] without changing total body K+ (internal-balance arm)"
    .
