<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepatic_urate_production> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_urate> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Ahepatic_urate_production%3Apositive%3Aplasma_urate> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepatic_urate_production> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_urate> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; dcterms:source "Boron & Boulpaep Medical Physiology (purine catabolism / uric acid); Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (purine degradation, xanthine oxidase pathway in liver); Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine, hyperuricemia/gout chapter (urate overproduction)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "the liver is the dominant site of net uric acid production (terminal purine catabolism); higher hepatic urate output raises the circulating urate pool at fixed renal clearance (source term of the urate mass balance)"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/renal_urate_excretion> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_urate> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Arenal_urate_excretion%3Anegative%3Aplasma_urate> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/renal_urate_excretion> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_urate> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; dcterms:source "Boron & Boulpaep Medical Physiology (renal urate handling, URAT1/SLC22A12, GLUT9/SLC2A9); Harrison's Nephrology and Acid-Base Disorders (uric acid excretion); renal hypouricemia OMIM 220150"
    ; pmo:mechanism "the kidney clears ~two-thirds of the daily urate load; net renal urate excretion (filtration minus URAT1/GLUT9-mediated reabsorption plus secretion) is the dominant sink, so higher excretion lowers steady-state plasma urate"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/xanthine_oxidase_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepatic_urate_production> .
