    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (xanthine oxidase, purine degradation); Boron & Boulpaep Medical Physiology; Harrison's (allopurinol xanthine-oxidase inhibition lowers urate)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "xanthine oxidoreductase (XDH/XO) catalyses hypoxanthine -> xanthine -> uric acid, the final and rate-limiting steps of purine catabolism; greater XO activity raises hepatic urate production (basis of allopurinol/febuxostat urate-lowering therapy)"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/purine_synthesis_rate> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepatic_urate_production> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Apurine_synthesis_rate%3Apositive%3Ahepatic_urate_production> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/purine_synthesis_rate> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepatic_urate_production> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (de-novo purine biosynthesis, PRPP-amidotransferase committed step); PRPP synthetase (PRPS1) superactivity OMIM 300661 (purine overproduction -> hyperuricemia); Harrison's hyperuricemia/gout; StatPearls Lesch-Nyhan NBK556079 (opened: de-novo purine synthesis via PRPP -> IMP -> hypoxanthine -> uric acid; PRPS1 superactivity gain-of-function OMIM 300661 -> purine/urate overproduction)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "de-novo purine biosynthesis (committed step is PRPP + glutamine -> phosphoribosylamine by PRPP-amidotransferase) expands the purine-nucleotide pool whose turnover terminates in uric acid; overproduction (e.g. PRPS1 superactivity) raises urate output"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/purine_synthesis_rate> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_xanthine> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Apurine_synthesis_rate%3Apositive%3Aplasma_xanthine> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/purine_synthesis_rate> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_xanthine> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (purine biosynthesis -> nucleotide turnover -> hypoxanthine/xanthine); Boron & Boulpaep Medical Physiology; StatPearls Lesch-Nyhan NBK556079 (opened: de-novo synthesis and unsalvaged purines feed hypoxanthine/xanthine before catabolism to uric acid)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "increased de-novo purine production raises the upstream substrate pool (hypoxanthine/xanthine) entering catabolism, raising their plasma levels at fixed downstream XO activity"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hgprt_activity> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/purine_synthesis_rate> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Ahgprt_activity%3Anegative%3Apurine_synthesis_rate> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hgprt_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/purine_synthesis_rate> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (purine salvage, HGPRT, PRPP availability and feedback inhibition of de-novo synthesis); Lesch-Nyhan HPRT1 OMIM 300322; Harrison's (HGPRT deficiency -> purine overproduction)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "HGPRT salvages hypoxanthine/guanine using PRPP back to nucleotides; high HGPRT activity consumes PRPP and replenishes purine nucleotides that feed back to inhibit PRPP-amidotransferase, so it SUPPRESSES de-novo synthesis. HGPRT loss (Lesch-Nyhan) raises PRPP and de-represses de-novo synthesis (negative edge)"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hgprt_activity> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepatic_urate_production> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Ahgprt_activity%3Anegative%3Ahepatic_urate_production> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hgprt_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepatic_urate_production> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (salvage vs catabolic fate of hypoxanthine/guanine); Lesch-Nyhan HPRT1 OMIM 300322 (HGPRT loss -> uric acid overproduction); Harrison's hyperuricemia/gout"
    ; pmo:mechanism "hypoxanthine/guanine not salvaged by HGPRT are diverted into the xanthine-oxidase catabolic pathway to uric acid; loss of HGPRT (Lesch-Nyhan) routes more substrate to urate, so HGPRT activity is inversely related to urate production"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hgprt_activity> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_xanthine> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Ahgprt_activity%3Anegative%3Aplasma_xanthine> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hgprt_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_xanthine> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (HGPRT salvage of hypoxanthine/guanine); Lesch-Nyhan HPRT1 OMIM 300322; Boron & Boulpaep Medical Physiology; StatPearls Lesch-Nyhan NBK556079 (opened: HPRT loss of function -> accumulation of hypoxanthine and xanthine diverted to catabolism; HPRT1 LoF OMIM 300322 = natural do())"
    ; pmo:mechanism "HGPRT salvage consumes hypoxanthine/guanine; reduced HGPRT activity (Lesch-Nyhan) leaves more hypoxanthine/xanthine for catabolism, raising the upstream xanthine/hypoxanthine pool (inverse relation)"
    .
