    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "\"Pulsatile GnRH administration normalizes pulsatile LH but not testosterone secretion, consistent with an impairment of hypothalamic GnRH secretion occurring in combination with a primary defect in testosterone production by the testis\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 19, p. 724"
    ; pmo:mechanism "pulsatile GnRH stimulates pituitary gonadotroph LH secretion; exogenous pulsatile GnRH administration normalizes pulsatile LH"
    .
