    ; pmo:causalEvidence "perturbation"
    ; dcterms:source "Wong, Cells: Molecules and Mechanisms §wong-7.7 (Telomeres - Undeclared): 'The activity of telomerase is primarily regulated by expression of the TERT gene (telomerase reverse transcriptase)'"
    ; pmo:mechanism "TERT gene encodes the catalytic reverse-transcriptase subunit of the telomerase holoenzyme; more TERT expression produces more functional telomerase enzyme"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/telomerase_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/telomere_length> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Atelomerase_activity%3Apositive%3Atelomere_length> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/telomerase_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/telomere_length> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "perturbation"
    ; dcterms:source "Wong, Cells: Molecules and Mechanisms §wong-7.7 (Telomeres - Undeclared): 'Telomerase is a large holoenzyme that acts as a reverse transcriptase, reading a self-contained RNA template to add on telomere sequence to the 3’ ends of linear chromosomes' and 'while telomerases are active, the 3’ ends can be extended'"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Telomerase acts as a reverse transcriptase reading its self-contained RNA template to add telomeric repeat sequences to the 3' ends of linear chromosomes, thereby extending telomere length"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/helper_t_cell_activation> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/b_cell_proliferation> .
