    ; dcterms:source "OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-081 (15.3: Autonomic Reflexes and Homeostasis): 'The hormones released from the adrenal medulla—epinephrine and norepinephrine—will also bind to these receptors [adrenergic receptors on blood vessels], causing constriction and increasing blood pressure.' | textbook corroboration: OpenStax Biology 2e §bio-41.5 (41.5: Hormonal Control of Osmoregulatory Functions): 'These hormones [epinephrine and norepinephrine] function by acting directly on the smooth muscles of blood vessels to constrict them.'"
    ; pmo:mechanism "circulating epinephrine from the adrenal medulla binds adrenergic receptors on systemic blood vessel walls, causing smooth muscle constriction and raising vascular resistance"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/stomach_volume> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/stomach_motility> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Astomach_volume%3Apositive%3Astomach_motility> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/stomach_volume> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/stomach_motility> ; pmo:sign "+"
