    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-091 (17.4: The Pituitary Gland and Hypothalamus): 'elevated levels of thyroid hormones in the bloodstream then trigger a drop in production of TRH and subsequently TSH.' | textbook corroboration: OpenStax Biology 2e §bio-37.4 (37.4: Regulation of Hormone Production): increasing blood T3/T4 inhibit both pituitary and hypothalamus signaling in a negative feedback loop"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Elevated thyroid hormone levels feed back to suppress hypothalamic TRH production, completing the HPT negative-feedback loop."
