    ; dcterms:source "OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-094 (17.7: The Adrenal Glands): 'The androgens produced in the zona reticularis supplement the gonadal androgens. They are produced in response to ACTH from the anterior pituitary.'"
    ; pmo:mechanism "ACTH stimulates adrenal zona reticularis to produce androgens (DHEA, androstenedione), which are then converted peripherally to testosterone or estrogens"
