    ; dcterms:source "OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-100 (18.2: An Overview of Blood): 'albumin…its presence holds water inside the blood vessels and draws water from the tissues, across blood vessel walls, and into the bloodstream. This in turn helps to maintain both blood volume and blood pressure.'"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Albumin raises plasma colloid oncotic pressure, drawing water from interstitial tissues across capillary walls into the bloodstream, thereby expanding plasma (and blood) volume."
    .
