    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-103 (18.5: Leukocytes and Platelets): 'thrombopoietin, a glycoprotein secreted by the kidneys and liver, stimulates the proliferation of megakaryoblasts, which mature into megakaryocytes…[which] release into the circulation thousands of cytoplasmic fragments' (platelets)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Thrombopoietin stimulates proliferation of megakaryoblasts, which mature into megakaryocytes that release thousands of platelet fragments into the circulation"
    .
