    ; pmo:causalEvidence "mechanistic_model"
    ; dcterms:source "OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-136 (23.7: Accessory Organs in Digestion- The Liver, Pancreas, and Gallbladder): 'sodium bicarbonate...serves to buffer the acidic gastric juice in chyme'; 'the pancreas secretes just enough bicarbonate to counterbalance the amount of HCl produced in the stomach'"
    ; pmo:mechanism "bicarbonate secreted into the duodenum neutralizes acidic chyme, reducing luminal acidity"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_secretin> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_bile_acids> .
