    ; pmo:causalEvidence "perturbation"
    ; dcterms:source "OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-136 (23.7: Accessory Organs in Digestion- The Liver, Pancreas, and Gallbladder): 'bile production increases when fatty chyme enters the duodenum and stimulates the secretion of the gut hormone secretin'"
    ; pmo:mechanism "secretin (triggered by fatty chyme) stimulates bile production and release from the liver"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/lean_body_mass> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/metabolic_rate> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Alean_body_mass%3Apositive%3Ametabolic_rate> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/lean_body_mass> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/metabolic_rate> ; pmo:sign "+"
