    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-164 (28.3: Embryonic Development): 'The trophoblast secretes human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG), a hormone that directs the corpus luteum to survive, enlarge, and continue producing progesterone and estrogen to suppress menses.'"
    ; pmo:mechanism "hCG secreted by trophoblast stimulates the corpus luteum to maintain steroidogenesis and estrogen (estradiol) production during early pregnancy"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/alveolar_surfactant_amount> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/alveolar_surface_tension> .
