    ; pmo:causalEvidence "perturbation"
    ; dcterms:source "OpenStax Biology 2e §bio-34.1 (34.1: Digestive Systems): 'Hydrochloric acid helps to convert the inactive pepsinogen to pepsin.'"
    ; pmo:mechanism "HCl secreted by parietal cells acidifies the gastric lumen, converting inactive pepsinogen (secreted by chief cells) to active pepsin A via autocatalytic cleavage; the more acid, the more efficient the activation"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/gastric_pepsin_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/gastric_pepsin_activity> .
