    ; dcterms:source "OpenStax Biology 2e §bio-34.1 (34.1: Digestive Systems): 'Pepsin breaks peptide bonds and cleaves proteins into smaller polypeptides; it also helps activate more pepsinogen, starting a positive feedback mechanism that generates more pepsin.'"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Active pepsin cleaves its own precursor pepsinogen, generating more pepsin — a positive autocatalytic feedback loop within the gastric lumen"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_glucose> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/adipose_tissue_mass> .
