    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "OpenStax Biology 2e §bio-37.5 (37.5: Endocrine Glands): 'It acts in the bones to inhibit osteoclast activity and in the kidneys to stimulate excretion of calcium. The combination of these two events lowers body fluid levels of calcium.'"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Calcitonin acts on kidney tubules to stimulate calcium excretion, increasing urinary calcium output."
