    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "OpenStax Biology 2e §bio-38.4 (38.4: Muscle Contraction and Locomotion): 'ACh is broken down by the enzyme acetylcholinesterase (AChE) into acetyl and choline. AChE resides in the synaptic cleft, breaking down ACh so that it does not remain bound to ACh receptors.'"
    ; pmo:mechanism "AChE hydrolyzes acetylcholine into acetate and choline in the synaptic cleft, reducing ACh availability to bind nicotinic receptors at the motor end plate"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/respiratory_rate> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/alveolar_ventilation> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Arespiratory_rate%3Apositive%3Aalveolar_ventilation> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/respiratory_rate> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/alveolar_ventilation> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "mechanistic_model"
    ; dcterms:source "OpenStax Biology 2e §bio-39.3 (39.3: Breathing): 'The respiratory rate contributes to the alveolar ventilation, or how much air moves into and out of the alveoli.'"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Breathing faster increases the total volume of air moved into and out of the alveoli per minute, directly raising alveolar ventilation (VA = RR x [VT - VD])."
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/tidal_volume> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/alveolar_ventilation> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Atidal_volume%3Apositive%3Aalveolar_ventilation> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/tidal_volume> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/alveolar_ventilation> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "mechanistic_model"
    ; dcterms:source "OpenStax Biology 2e §bio-39.3 (39.3: Breathing): 'There are two ways to keep the alveolar ventilation constant: increase the respiratory rate while decreasing the tidal volume of air per breath (shallow breathing), or decrease the respiratory rate while increasing the tidal volume per breath.' — showing tidal volume and respiratory rate both determine ventilation."
    ; pmo:mechanism "Larger tidal volume per breath increases total air moved through alveoli per minute, raising effective alveolar ventilation independently of rate."
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/arterial_pco2> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_bicarbonate> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aarterial_pco2%3Apositive%3Aplasma_bicarbonate> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/arterial_pco2> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_bicarbonate> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "Whenever the P CO2 rises, the bicarbonate must also increase to some extent because of dissociation of the carbonic acid produced"
    ; pmo:mechanism "a rise in PCO2 drives dissociation of carbonic acid, increasing plasma bicarbonate (in vitro buffer-line slope)"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/blood_carbon_monoxide> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hemoglobin_o2_saturation> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Ablood_carbon_monoxide%3Anegative%3Ahemoglobin_o2_saturation> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/blood_carbon_monoxide> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hemoglobin_o2_saturation> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "perturbation"
    ; dcterms:source "OpenStax Biology 2e §bio-39.4 (39.4: Transport of Gases in Human Bodily Fluids): 'Carbon monoxide has a greater affinity for hemoglobin than oxygen. Therefore, when carbon monoxide is present, it binds to hemoglobin preferentially over oxygen. As a result, oxygen cannot bind to hemoglobin, so very little oxygen is transported through the body… as percent CO increases, the oxygen saturation of hemoglobin decreases.'"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Carbon monoxide binds hemoglobin with ~250-fold higher affinity than oxygen, occupying heme sites and competitively preventing O2 binding; raised blood CO concentration displaces oxygen from hemoglobin, reducing SaO2"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_vitamin_k> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/thrombin> .
