    ; pmo:mechanism "CO2 binds covalently to Hb N-terminus forming a negatively charged carbamate that salt-bridges with Arg 141, stabilizing the T (deoxy) state and lowering Hb-O2 affinity; higher PaCO2 increases [H+] (carbonic acid equilibrium) further reinforcing T-state stabilization"
    .
