    ; pmo:mechanism "Heparin binds a specific site on antithrombin III, inducing a conformational change that increases antithrombin's efficacy as a thrombin inhibitor; heparin also facilitates 1D diffusion of thrombin along the polyanion chain to find antithrombin, accelerating inhibition"
