    ; dcterms:source "HumMod thyroid module (TSH -> T4 secretion rate); Degon 2008 HPT model | textbook corroboration: OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-090 (17.3: Hormones): table entry 'TSH: Stimulates thyroid hormone release'; OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-091 (17.4: The Pituitary Gland and Hypothalamus): 'It [TSH] triggers the secretion of thyroid hormones by the thyroid gland.'; OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-092 (17.5: The Thyroid Gland): 'TSH stimulates the thyroid gland to secrete T3 and T4'; OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-166 (28.5: Changes During Pregnancy, Labor, and Birth): 'Thyrotropin, in conjunction with placental hormones, increases the production of thyroid hormone, which raises the maternal metabolic rate.'; OpenStax Biology 2e §bio-37.3 (37.3: Regulation of Body Processes): 'T3 and T4 release from the thyroid gland is stimulated by thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH)'; 'TSH binding at the receptors of the follicle of the thyroid triggers the production of T3 and T4 from a glycoprotein called thyroglobulin.'; OpenStax Biology 2e §bio-37.4 (37.4: Regulation of Hormone Production): anterior pituitary TSH stimulates the thyroid gland to produce T3 and T4 (hormonal stimulus example)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "TSH stimulates thyroidal T4 synthesis and secretion (TSH-receptor / cAMP)"
    .
