    ; dcterms:source "\"the rate of TSH secretion is exquisitely sensitive to the plasma concentrations of free thyroid hormones\" and \"Because the concentration of TSH is inversely proportional to the degree of thyroid hormone excess, patients with clinical symptoms almost invariably have serum TSH concentrations below 0.1 mU/L.\" Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 11, p. 356/358"
    ; pmo:mechanism "free T4 (and T3) exert negative feedback on thyrotrophs; TSH concentration is inversely proportional to free thyroid hormone supply"
    .
