    ; pmo:causalEvidence "mechanistic_model"
    ; dcterms:source "Degon 2008 HPT feedback; classic thyroid-hormone negative feedback | textbook corroboration: OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-092 (17.5: The Thyroid Gland): 'increasing levels of T3 and T4 decrease the production and secretion of TSH' (negative feedback); OpenStax Biology 2e §bio-37.3 (37.3: Regulation of Body Processes): 'Increased T3 and T4 levels in the blood inhibit the release of TSH, which results in lower T3 and T4 release from the thyroid.'; OpenStax Biology 2e §bio-37.4 (37.4: Regulation of Hormone Production): rising T3/T4 blood concentrations inhibit both the pituitary and hypothalamus in a negative feedback loop"
    ; pmo:mechanism "T3 directly inhibits pituitary thyrotroph TSH secretion (TRb feedback)"
    .
