<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/free_t3> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/metabolic_rate> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Afree_t3%3Apositive%3Ametabolic_rate> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/free_t3> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/metabolic_rate> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "mechanistic_model"
    ; dcterms:source "Boron & Boulpaep endocrine physiology; HumMod metabolism (T3 -> metabolic rate) | textbook corroboration: OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-005 (1.6: Homeostasis): 'The brain triggers the thyroid gland in the endocrine system to release thyroid hormone, which increases metabolic activity and heat production in cells throughout the body'; OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-092 (17.5: The Thyroid Gland): 'T3 and T4 are often referred to as metabolic hormones because their levels influence the body's basal metabolic rate'; OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-099 (17.12: Development and Aging of the Endocrine System): 'the thyroid gland produces less of the thyroid hormones, causing a gradual decrease in the basal metabolic rate'.; OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-143 (24.7: Energy and Heat Balance): thyroid hormone stimulates more energy use and heat production by cells throughout the body; OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-166 (28.5: Changes During Pregnancy, Labor, and Birth): 'Thyrotropin...increases the production of thyroid hormone, which raises the maternal metabolic rate.'; OpenStax Biology 2e §bio-37.2 (37.2: How Hormones Work): 'thyroid hormones act on many different tissue types, stimulating metabolic activity throughout the body.'; OpenStax Biology 2e §bio-37.3 (37.3: Regulation of Body Processes): 'T3 and T4 activate genes involved in energy production and glucose oxidation. This results in increased rates of metabolism and body heat production, which is known as the hormone's calorigenic effect.'"
    ; pmo:mechanism "T3 raises basal metabolic rate (Na/K-ATPase, mitochondrial uncoupling, calorigenesis)"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/free_t3> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/sa_node_automaticity> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Afree_t3%3Apositive%3Asa_node_automaticity> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/free_t3> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/sa_node_automaticity> ; pmo:sign "+"
