    ; pmo:mechanism "hepatocyte ATP7B pumps copper into the bile canaliculus for biliary excretion (the major route of copper elimination); ATP7B loss-of-function abolishes biliary copper efflux and copper accumulates in the liver"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/atp7b_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_ceruloplasmin> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aatp7b_activity%3Apositive%3Aplasma_ceruloplasmin> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/atp7b_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_ceruloplasmin> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "OMIM #277900 Wilson disease (low serum ceruloplasmin); Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry (ceruloplasmin copper loading); Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine"
    ; pmo:mechanism "ATP7B in the hepatocyte trans-Golgi network loads copper onto apoceruloplasmin to form secreted holo-ceruloplasmin; without copper loading, apoceruloplasmin is rapidly degraded, so ATP7B loss lowers circulating (holo-)ceruloplasmin"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepatic_copper_excretion> obo:RO_0002411 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_copper> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Ahepatic_copper_excretion%3Aunknown%3Aplasma_copper> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepatic_copper_excretion> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_copper> ; pmo:sign "?"
    ; dcterms:source "Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine (Wilson disease: low total serum copper, raised free copper, hepatic accumulation); Boron & Boulpaep Medical Physiology"
    ; pmo:mechanism "hepatobiliary excretion removes copper from the body; in isolation higher excretion lowers the body copper pool, but in Wilson disease loss of excretion paradoxically LOWERS measured (ceruloplasmin-bound) serum copper while raising hepatic/free copper — the net sign on the ceruloplasmin-bound plasma pool is dominated by ceruloplasmin, so this direct edge is flagged ambiguous"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_ceruloplasmin> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_copper> .
