    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "AOP-Wiki KER 895c39c8-3235-4c89-8d25-f1eef024ad3f; AOP: 'Antagonist binding to PPARα leading to body-weight loss' — KER direction: decreased circulating ketone bodies -> increased catabolism of muscle protein (organ UBERON:0002204); interventionist sign: do(ketone bodies up) -> muscle catabolism down (sign -) | No PMID in batch | *** DRAFT FOR REVIEW (imported) ***"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Circulating ketone bodies (acetoacetate, 3-hydroxybutyrate) suppress ubiquitin-proteasome-mediated muscle protein catabolism during fasting; low ketone availability removes this inhibitory signal and increases muscle proteolysis"
