    ; dcterms:source "AOP-Wiki KER uuid 080d59cc-c252-46c4-a825-aca547b579ef; AOP: 'HMG-CoA reductase inhibition leading to decreased fertility'. No PMID supplied. Mechanism: statins reduce cholesterol -> reduced steroidogenesis substrate -> reduced testosterone (Dobs et al., J Clin Endocrinol Metab 2000; PMID not verified — using AOP-Wiki KER as provenance). Sign '+': increased cholesterol increases testosterone. *** DRAFT FOR REVIEW (imported) ***"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Plasma cholesterol is the obligate precursor for all steroid hormones. Leydig cells import cholesterol via StAR (steroidogenic acute regulatory protein); cholesterol is converted by CYP11A1 (side-chain cleavage enzyme) to pregnenolone, then to testosterone via the steroidogenic cascade. Reduced plasma cholesterol substrate limits testosterone synthesis."
    .
