    ; pmo:mechanism "Thyroid hormones (free T4/T3) maintain glomerular filtration rate (GFR) via multiple mechanisms: thyroid hormone increases renal expression of Na/K-ATPase and eNOS, maintains cardiac output and renal perfusion, and reduces tubular creatinine reabsorption. Hypothyroidism reduces GFR, impairing creatinine clearance and elevating serum creatinine."
    .
