    ; dcterms:source "AOP-Wiki KER 4988fd83-79f6-4a25-9ce9-31575e55f095; AOP: 'Iodotyrosine deiodinase (IYD) inhibition leading to altered amphibian metamorphosis'. No PMID provided. pmid_ok=false. Human genetic grounding: IYD deficiency (homozygous IYD loss-of-function mutations Q6PHW0) causes urinary iodine wasting and hypothyroidism (Moreno et al., NEJM 2008), confirming interventional (genetic_lof_gof) evidence. INDRA: IYD has 217 total statements but 0 specific IYD->thyroidal_iodide pairs. *** DRAFT FOR REVIEW (imported) ***"
    ; pmo:mechanism "IYD (iodotyrosine deiodinase 1) catalyzes deiodination of MIT and DIT back to iodide + tyrosine within thyroid follicular cells; when IYD activity is higher, more iodide is recycled from iodotyrosine intermediates, enlarging the intracellular thyroidal iodide pool available for TPO-catalyzed organification (quality: IYD catalytic activity -> disposition: iodotyrosine hydrolysis -> process: iodide salvage -> quality: thyroidal iodide concentration)"
    .
