    ; dcterms:source "AOP-Wiki KER 5d76797b-5e3c-4fd5-9805-69faff17190a; AOP: 'Pendrin inhibition leading to altered amphibian metamorphosis'. No PMID provided. pmid_ok=false. Human genetic grounding: SLC26A4 (pendrin) biallelic loss-of-function mutations cause Pendred syndrome (sensorineural deafness + goiter/hypothyroidism, OMIM #274600), demonstrating that pendrin is required for normal thyroid hormone synthesis in humans (genetic_lof_gof). INDRA: SLC26A4->TPO: 3 statements (cross-confirming). *** DRAFT FOR REVIEW (imported) ***"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Pendrin (SLC26A4) transports iodide across the apical membrane of thyroid follicular cells into the follicular lumen, where it serves as substrate for TPO-catalyzed organification (iodination of thyroglobulin tyrosine residues). Pendrin activity up -> more luminal iodide -> higher iodide-organification capacity (quality: pendrin transport activity -> disposition: apical iodide efflux -> process: luminal iodide accumulation -> quality: TPO/NIS organification capacity)"
    .
