    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "AOP-Wiki KER uuid 2f234598-bda7-42a8-bf7f-971319c7b317; AOP: 'Peroxisome proliferator-activated receptor alpha activation leading to early life stage mortality via reduced ATP'. No PMID provided (pmid_ok=false, pmid_concordant=false). AOP context is ecotox but the KER mechanism is conserved mammalian physiology (PPARα-driven FAO induction is the fasting-state and fibrate-drug mechanism in humans). INDRA: PPARA->CPT1A Activation×2 + IncreaseAmount×4 (6 same-direction statements) independently confirm. PR:Q07869 and GO:0006635 verified in offline OBO files. *** DRAFT FOR REVIEW (imported) ***"
    ; pmo:mechanism "PPARα acts as a nuclear receptor transcription factor; upon activation by fatty acid ligands (or fibrate drugs), it directly induces CPT1A, HADHA and other FAO-cycle genes, increasing hepatic mitochondrial fatty acid β-oxidation flux"
    .
