    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "AOP-Wiki KER uuid 4cb2965c-c618-4264-b78f-6210ae959076; AOPs: 'Increased 11β-Hydroxysteroid dehydrogenase type 1 activity leading to MASLD progression via lipogenesis-associated mitochondrial dysfunction' and two related MASLD lipogenesis AOPs. No PMID supplied in batch entry (pmid_ok=false, pmid_concordant=false). KER curated as mechanistic (GR -> lipogenic gene transcription). INDRA independently confirms NR3C1->FASN IncreaseAmount (PMID:30776459, 38481602) and NR3C1-FASN-ACACA-SCD1 promoter ChIP (PMID:29331496). *** DRAFT FOR REVIEW (imported) ***"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Glucocorticoid receptor (NR3C1) activation in hepatocytes drives transcription of lipogenic genes (FASN, ACACA, SCD1), increasing de novo fatty acid biosynthesis flux. GR binds promoter regions of these enzymes directly and via SREBP1c co-activation."
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/ppara_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepatic_ketogenesis> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Appara_activity%3Apositive%3Ahepatic_ketogenesis> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/ppara_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepatic_ketogenesis> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "perturbation"
    ; dcterms:source "perturbation do(): Ppara global knockout in mouse under fasting/starvation challenge. Intervention: PPARalpha-null; measured endpoint: failure to induce the hepatic FAO/HMGCS2 program on fasting -> hypoketonaemia (with steatosis and hypoglycaemia); context: mouse, hepatic, fasting transcriptional program. do(PPARalpha down) -> ketogenesis down, so activity up -> ketogenesis up (sign +). Corroborated pharmacologically by fibrate (PPARalpha agonist) induction of hepatic FAO/ketogenesis genes. PMID:10359558 (Kersten S et al., J Clin Invest 1999;103:1489-1498); PMID:10377439 (Leone TC et al., PNAS 1999;96:7473-7478). Distinct target from the existing ppara_activity -(+)-> hepatic_fa_beta_oxidation_rate edge. *** DRAFT FOR REVIEW ***"
    ; pmo:mechanism "PPARalpha transactivates the hepatic fasting fatty-acid-oxidation / ketogenesis program (CPT1, mitochondrial HMG-CoA synthase 2 [HMGCS2], the beta-oxidation gene battery) in hepatocytes, setting ketogenic flux capacity"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/fxr_activity> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/cyp7a1_activity> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Afxr_activity%3Anegative%3Acyp7a1_activity> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/fxr_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/cyp7a1_activity> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "pharmacological do(): FXR synthetic agonist GW4064 (and bile-acid ligands / obeticholic acid) in hepatocytes and mouse liver. Intervention: FXR agonism; measured endpoint: SHP induction with repressed CYP7A1 transcription/activity -> reduced bile-acid synthesis; context: mouse/human hepatocyte, sub-acute transcriptional repression. do(FXR up) -> CYP7A1 down (sign -). PMID:11030332 (Goodwin B et al., Mol Cell 2000;6:517-526 — the FXR-SHP-LRH-1 cascade). *** DRAFT FOR REVIEW ***"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Ligand-activated FXR (NR1H4) induces SHP (NR0B2), which represses LRH-1/HNF4 at the CYP7A1 promoter, lowering CYP7A1 (cholesterol 7alpha-hydroxylase) transcription and activity — the rate-limiting enzyme of the neutral bile-acid synthesis pathway"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_bile_acids> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/fxr_activity> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aplasma_bile_acids%3Apositive%3Afxr_activity> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_bile_acids> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/fxr_activity> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "pharmacological do(): endogenous bile-acid ligands (CDCA/DCA/LCA) and synthetic FXR agonists (obeticholic acid ~100x CDCA potency; GW4064) activate the FXR/NR1H4 receptor. Intervention: bile-acid / agonist ligand exposure; measured endpoint: FXR-RXR transcriptional activation at physiological bile-acid concentrations; context: human/rodent nuclear-receptor pharmacology. do(bile acids up) -> FXR transcriptional activity up (sign +). PMID:10334992 (Makishima M et al., Science 1999;284:1362-1365); PMID:10334993 (Parks DJ et al., Science 1999;284:1365-1368); PMID:10360171 (Wang H et al., Mol Cell 1999;3:543-553). *** DRAFT FOR REVIEW ***"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Bile acids (CDCA, DCA, LCA) are the endogenous agonists of the nuclear receptor FXR (NR1H4); raising plasma / enterohepatic bile-acid concentration activates FXR-RXR-dependent transcription (induces SHP/FGF19, represses CYP7A1)"
    .
