<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aglutamate_dehydrogenase_activity%3Apositive%3Aplasma_ammonia> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/glutamate_dehydrogenase_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_ammonia> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "Hyperinsulinism-hyperammonemia syndrome (HI/HA), OMIM:606762 — GLUD1 GoF causes hyperammonemia; plasma ammonia chronically elevated (100-200 μmol/L) due to over-active glutamate dehydrogenase; the same edge direction applies: more GLUD1 activity -> more ammonia"
    ; pmo:mechanism "RHEA:11612 (EC 1.4.1.3): L-glutamate + NADP(+) + H2O = 2-oxoglutarate + NH4(+) + NADPH + H(+); NH4+ (ammonia) is the direct product; GLUD1 gain-of-function (activating mutation) increases enzyme flux and NH4+ production; edge sign reflects enzyme_activity -> product relationship (applicable for both GoF assessment and the underlying physiology)"
    .
