<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aglutamate_dehydrogenase_activity%3Anegative%3Aplasma_glutamine> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/glutamate_dehydrogenase_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_glutamine> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "Hyperinsulinism-hyperammonemia syndrome (HI/HA), OMIM:606762 — GLUD1 GoF increases glutamate catabolism; plasma glutamine may be mildly reduced or normal; edge encodes the physiological relationship (more enzyme -> less substrate)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "RHEA:11612 (EC 1.4.1.3): L-glutamate + NADP(+) + H2O = 2-oxoglutarate + NH4(+) + NADPH; L-glutamate is the substrate; increased GLUD1 flux (GoF) depletes glutamate; glutamate is the immediate precursor of glutamine (via glutamine synthetase) so glutamate depletion leads to relative glutamine reduction or prevents its rise"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/methionine_synthase_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_methionine> .
