    ; dcterms:source "\"If the alveolar ventilation is halved (and CO2 production remains unchanged), for example, the alveolar and arterial PCO2 will double\" (West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 2)  ||  \"if the alveolar ventilation is halved, the P 2 is doubled, once a steady state has been established.\" — West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 5"
