    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "\"With heavy exercise, the pulmonary blood flow is greatly increased, and the time normally spent by the red cell in the capillary, about 0.75 s, may be reduced to as little as one-third of this\" (West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 3)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "increased pulmonary blood flow reduces the time a red cell spends in the capillary"
    .
