    ; dcterms:source "\"theta for CO is reduced if a subject breathes a high O2 mixture, because the O2 competes with the CO for hemoglobin. As a result, the measured diffusing capacity is reduced by O2 breathing\" (West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 3)"
