    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "Figure 4.4 shows that an increase in either pulmonary arterial or venous pressure causes pulmonary vascular resistance to fall. ... As the pressure rises, these vessels begin to conduct blood, thus lowering the overall resistance. This is termed recruitment"
    ; pmo:mechanism "raising arterial perfusing pressure recruits closed capillaries and distends open ones, lowering resistance"
    .
