<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/alveolar_ventilation> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/alveolar_po2> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aalveolar_ventilation%3Apositive%3Aalveolar_po2> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/alveolar_ventilation> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/alveolar_po2> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "\"if the alveolar ventilation is abnormally low, the alveolar P 2 falls. ... In practice, therefore, the alveolar P 2 is largely determined by the level of alveolar ventilation.\" — West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 5"
    ; pmo:mechanism "alveolar PO2 set by balance of O2 removal by blood vs replenishment by ventilation; raising ventilation raises alveolar PO2"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/alveolar_pco2> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/arterial_pco2> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aalveolar_pco2%3Apositive%3Aarterial_pco2> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/alveolar_pco2> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/arterial_pco2> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "\"Hypoventilation always causes an increased alveolar and, therefore, arterial P 2.\" — West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 5"
    ; pmo:mechanism "arterial PCO2 equilibrates with alveolar PCO2 across the blood-gas barrier; a rise in alveolar PCO2 raises arterial PCO2"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/alveolar_po2> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/arterial_po2> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aalveolar_po2%3Apositive%3Aarterial_po2> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/alveolar_po2> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/arterial_po2> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "\"Hypoventilation always reduces the alveolar and arterial P 2 except when the subject breathes an enriched O2 mixture.\" — West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 5"
    ; pmo:mechanism "end-capillary/arterial PO2 equilibrates with alveolar PO2; lowering alveolar PO2 lowers arterial PO2"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/arterial_po2> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/tissue_po2> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aarterial_po2%3Apositive%3Atissue_po2> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/arterial_po2> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/tissue_po2> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "\"any decrease of P 2 in arterial blood must result in a lower tissue P 2 other things being equal. For the same reasons, impaired pulmonary gas exchange causes a rise in tissue P 2.\" — West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 5"
    ; pmo:mechanism "the lung is a link in the O2 transport chain; arterial PO2 sets the gradient driving O2 diffusion to mitochondria, so lower arterial PO2 lowers tissue PO2"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/ventilation_perfusion_ratio> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/alveolar_po2> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aventilation_perfusion_ratio%3Apositive%3Aalveolar_po2> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/ventilation_perfusion_ratio> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/alveolar_po2> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "\"Now suppose that the ventilation-perfusion ratio of the unit is gradually reduced by obstructing its ventilation, leaving its blood flow unchanged ... It is clear that the O2 in the unit will fall ... Suppose instead that the ventilation-perfusion ratio is increased by decreasing blood flow ... Now the O2 rises\" — West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 5"
    ; pmo:mechanism "alveolar PO2 of a unit is set by its V/Q ratio; reducing V/Q (obstructing ventilation, flow fixed) lowers O2; raising V/Q raises O2 toward inspired gas"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/ventilation_perfusion_ratio> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/alveolar_pco2> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aventilation_perfusion_ratio%3Anegative%3Aalveolar_pco2> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/ventilation_perfusion_ratio> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/alveolar_pco2> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "\"the ventilation-perfusion ratio of the unit is gradually reduced ... the CO2 will rise ... the ventilation-perfusion ratio is increased by decreasing blood flow ... the O2 rises and the CO2 falls\" — West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 5"
    ; pmo:mechanism "alveolar PCO2 of a unit is set by its V/Q ratio; reducing V/Q raises CO2 toward mixed venous, raising V/Q lowers CO2 toward inspired gas"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/pulmonary_shunt_fraction> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/arterial_po2> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Apulmonary_shunt_fraction%3Anegative%3Aarterial_po2> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/pulmonary_shunt_fraction> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/arterial_po2> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "\"The effect of the addition of this poorly oxygenated blood is to depress the arterial P 2. ... the shunted blood that bypasses ventilated alveoli is never exposed to the higher alveolar P 2, so it continues to depress the arterial P 2.\" — West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 5"
    ; pmo:mechanism "shunted poorly-oxygenated blood mixes into arterial blood without exposure to alveolar gas, depressing arterial PO2; effect grows with shunt fraction and is not abolished by 100% O2"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/arterial_ph> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hemoglobin_o2_affinity> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aarterial_ph%3Apositive%3Ahemoglobin_o2_affinity> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/arterial_ph> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hemoglobin_o2_affinity> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "The O2 dissociation curve is shifted to the right, that is, the O2 affinity of Hb is reduced, by an increase in H+ concentration  ||  \"The oxygen dissociation curve moves to the right in exercising muscles because of the increase in PCO2, H+ concentration, and temperature.\" (West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 9)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Bohr effect: an increase in H+ (lower pH) reduces O2 affinity (right shift); higher pH/lower H+ raises affinity"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/arterial_pco2> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hemoglobin_o2_affinity> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aarterial_pco2%3Anegative%3Ahemoglobin_o2_affinity> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/arterial_pco2> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hemoglobin_o2_affinity> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "The O2 dissociation curve is shifted to the right ... by an increase in H+ concentration, P CO2, temperature ... Most of the effect of P CO2, which is known as the Bohr effect, can be attributed to its action on H+ concentration  ||  \"The oxygen dissociation curve moves to the right in exercising muscles because of the increase in PCO2, H+ concentration, and temperature.\" (West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 9)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Bohr effect: a rise in PCO2 (largely via its action on H+) reduces hemoglobin O2 affinity, right-shifting the curve"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/core_temperature> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hemoglobin_o2_affinity> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Acore_temperature%3Anegative%3Ahemoglobin_o2_affinity> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/core_temperature> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hemoglobin_o2_affinity> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "The O2 dissociation curve is shifted to the right, that is, the O2 affinity of Hb is reduced, by an increase in H+ concentration, P CO2, temperature, and the concentration of 2,3-diphosphoglycerate  ||  \"The oxygen dissociation curve moves to the right in exercising muscles because of the increase in PCO2, H+ concentration, and temperature. This assists the unloading of oxygen to the muscles.\" (West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 9)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "a rise in temperature reduces hemoglobin O2 affinity (right shift)"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/erythrocyte_23_bpg> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hemoglobin_o2_affinity> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aerythrocyte_23_bpg%3Anegative%3Ahemoglobin_o2_affinity> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/erythrocyte_23_bpg> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hemoglobin_o2_affinity> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "An increase in 2,3-DPG, which is an end product of red cell metabolism, shifts the curve to the right ... the unloading of O2 to peripheral tissues is assisted  ||  \"There is a rightward shift of the O2 dissociation curve at moderate altitudes that results in a better unloading of O2 in venous blood at a given PO2. The cause of the shift is an increase in concentration of 2,3-diphosphoglycerate...\" (West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 9)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "increased red-cell 2,3-DPG reduces hemoglobin O2 affinity (right shift), assisting unloading"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hemoglobin_o2_affinity> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/peripheral_o2_unloading> .
