    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "A rightward shift means more unloading of O2 at a given P O2 in a tissue capillary ... By contrast, stored blood in a blood bank may be depleted of 2,3-DPG, which impairs unloading of O2"
    ; pmo:mechanism "lower O2 affinity (right-shifted curve) increases O2 unloading at a given tissue capillary PO2; higher affinity impairs unloading"
    .
