    ; pmo:mechanism "surface tension of the curved alveolar surface lowers hydrostatic pressure in peri-capillary tissue, sucking fluid out of the capillaries; surfactant (low surface tension) prevents transudation, so high surface tension promotes alveolar/interstitial fluid accumulation"
    .
