    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "An increase in arterial blood pressure can cause reflex hypoventilation or apnea through stimulation of the aortic and carotid sinus baroreceptors. Conversely, a decrease in blood pressure may result in hyperventilation"
