    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "\"Cardiac output increases approximately linearly with work level as a result of increases in both heart rate and stroke volume, with the latter increasing due to increases in venous return and cardiac inotropy.\" (West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 9)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "increased venous return raises end-diastolic filling (Frank-Starling), augmenting stroke volume"
    .
