    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "\"At higher altitudes, there is a leftward shift in the dissociation curve caused by the respiratory alkalosis, and this assists in the loading of O2 in the pulmonary capillaries.\" (West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 9)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "higher O2 affinity (leftward shift) increases hemoglobin saturation at a given PO2, assisting O2 loading"
    .
