    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "\"The ductus arteriosus begins to constrict a few minutes later in response to the direct action of the increased PO2 on its smooth muscle.\" (West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 9)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "a rise in PO2 acts directly on ductal smooth muscle to constrict it, reducing patency"
    .
