    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "\"This constriction is aided by reductions in the levels of local and circulating prostaglandins. Nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs can be given to inhibit prostaglandin synthesis and promote closure... prostaglandins are actually administered to infants... to keep the ductus open.\" (West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 9)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "prostaglandins relax/maintain ductal smooth muscle keeping it open; lowering prostaglandins (e.g. NSAID prostaglandin-synthesis inhibition) promotes closure"
    .
