    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "\"With the resulting increase in pulmonary blood flow, left atrial pressure rises and the flaplike foramen ovale quickly closes.\" (West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 9)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "increased pulmonary blood flow returning to the left atrium raises left atrial pressure"
    .
