    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "\"The FEV1.0 (or FEF25%–75%) is reduced by an increase in airway resistance or a reduction in elastic recoil of the lung\" (West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 10)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "increased airway resistance reduces maximal expiratory flow / FEV1.0 (flow = recoil pressure / upstream-segment resistance)"
    .
