    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "\"Pulmonary vascular endothelial cells also release potent vasoconstrictors such as endothelin-1 (ET-1) ... Endothelin receptor antagonists are now part of treatment regimens for many patients with pulmonary hypertension.\" (West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 4, Active Control of the Circulation)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "ET-1 secretion -> ETA/ETB receptor activation on pulmonary arterial smooth muscle -> rise in cytoplasmic Ca2+ -> vasoconstriction -> increased pulmonary vascular resistance"
    .
