    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "\"PKA also... the effects of antidiuretic hormone on the permeability of the renal collecting duct to water\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 2, p 28"
    ; pmo:mechanism "PKA (activated by ADH-stimulated cAMP) mediates aquaporin-2 insertion into apical membrane of collecting duct principal cells, raising water permeability (quality: ADH concentration → disposition: V2R/Gs/cAMP/PKA activation → process: AQP2 vesicle exocytosis → quality: collecting duct water permeability)"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/stat5_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepatic_igf1> .
