    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "\"Similar syndromes of decreased growth can also result from mutations in STAT5b and deficiency in IGF-1\" and \"STAT5b has been shown to dimerize with the glucocorticoid receptor, with the latter acting as a coactivator for STAT5b to promote expression of GH-regulated genes (e.g., IGF1) implicated in body growth.\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 2, p 26"
