    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "\"melatonin inhibits the activity of neurons in the SCN of the hypothalamus, the master circadian pacemaker in the mammalian brain... Targeted deletion (knockout) of the MT1, but not the MT2 receptor, abolished the ability of melatonin to inhibit the activity of SCN neurons\" Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 7, p. 126"
