    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "\"dopamine inhibits PRL secretion from lactotrophs both in vivo and in vitro, and dopamine D2 receptors are expressed on the plasma membrane of lactotrophs. Mutant mice with a targeted disruption of the D2 receptor gene uniformly develop lactotroph hyperplasia, hyperprolactinemia\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 7, p. 157-158"
