    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "\"dynorphin (or possibly enkephalin in humans), which inhibits kisspeptin secretion\" and \"treatment with a neurokinin B agonist and dynorphin antagonist can recover suppressed GnRH and LH secretion\" Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 7, p 166, 169"
    ; pmo:mechanism "dynorphin co-expressed in KNDy neurons inhibits kisspeptin secretion via kappa-opioid receptors; NK3R agonist plus dynorphin antagonist recovers suppressed GnRH/LH"
