    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "\"GABAergic neurons in the MnPO and MePO express the prostaglandin EP3 receptor, which when bound by PGE2 alters the thermoregulatory set-point and induces fever.\" Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 7, p 171"
    ; pmo:mechanism "PGE2 binds EP3 receptors on GABAergic neurons in MnPO/MePO, disinhibiting sympathoexcitatory neurons (DMN/rRPA) to increase BAT thermogenesis and shivering, raising body temperature (fever)"
