    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "\"administration of kisspeptin restored estrous cyclicity, ovulation, and circulating LH and FSH levels... kisspeptin administration to women with hyperprolactinemia-induced hypothalamic amenorrhea was shown to reactivate gonadotropin secretion.\" Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 8, p 193  ||  \"KISS1R, which encodes the receptor for kisspeptin 1/metastin, an important GnRH stimulatory neuropeptide particularly at the time of puberty (2–5%)\" [of CHH mutations] — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 19, p. 729"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Kisspeptin binds KISS1R on GnRH neurons → GnRH release; administration restores estrous cyclicity and gonadotropin secretion suppressed by hyperprolactinemia"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/estradiol> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/pituitary_prolactin_secretion> .
