    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "\"An increase in total circulating cholesterol and triglycerides is observed\"; \"Hepatic lipoprotein synthesis is stimulated, and increases in circulating cholesterol and triglycerides may be found\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 15, p. 496, 502  ||  \"Glucocorticoids have robust effects on multiple aspects of lipid metabolism, inducing expression of HMG-CoA reductase to promote cholesterol synthesis, increasing expression of fatty acid synthase to promote fatty acid synthesis, and decreasing LPL to impair clearance of circulating lipids. Accordingly, hyperlipidemia is commonly seen in the setting of glucocorticoid treatment.\" Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 41, p. 1587"
    ; pmo:mechanism "glucocorticoids increase lipolysis and stimulate hepatic lipoprotein synthesis → elevated circulating triglycerides"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/cyp21a2_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/zona_fasciculata_cortisol_secretion> .
