    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "\"75% of patients with classic 21-hydroxylase deficiency have clinically manifest mineralocorticoid deficiency because of failure to convert sufficient progesterone to DOC in the ZG.\" Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 15, p. 529"
    ; pmo:mechanism "CYP21A2 catalyses conversion of progesterone to 11-deoxycorticosterone (DOC) in zona glomerulosa; LoF blocks the aldosterone biosynthetic pathway, causing salt-wasting aldosterone deficiency"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/cyp11b1_activity> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_deoxycorticosterone> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Acyp11b1_activity%3Anegative%3Aplasma_deoxycorticosterone> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/cyp11b1_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_deoxycorticosterone> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "\"The condition arises because of mutations in the 11β-hydroxylase (CYP11B1) gene that result in loss of enzyme activity and a block in the conversion of 11-deoxycortisol to cortisol. ... The principal difference from 21-hydroxylase deficiency is hypertension, which is thought to be secondary to the mineralocorticoid effect of DOC excess.\" Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 15, p 534–535"
    ; pmo:mechanism "CYP11B1 (steroid 11β-hydroxylase) converts DOC to corticosterone; LoF blocks this step, causing DOC to accumulate"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_deoxycorticosterone> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/mean_arterial_pressure> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aplasma_deoxycorticosterone%3Apositive%3Amean_arterial_pressure> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_deoxycorticosterone> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/mean_arterial_pressure> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "\"The principal difference from 21-hydroxylase deficiency is hypertension, which is thought to be secondary to the mineralocorticoid effect of DOC excess. ... Accumulation of corticosterone and DOC results in severe hypokalemic hypertension.\" Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 15, p 535–536. Also confirmed by pharmacological reversal: \"Glucocorticoid replacement reverses the DOC-induced suppression of the renin-angiotensin system and lowers blood pressure.\" p 307.  ||  \"Excess DOC secretion eventually leads to hypertension, hypokalemic alkalosis, and suppression of the renin-angiotensin system\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 23, p 905"
    ; pmo:mechanism "DOC acts as a mineralocorticoid, promoting renal sodium/water retention and raising arterial blood pressure"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_deoxycorticosterone> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/renin> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aplasma_deoxycorticosterone%3Anegative%3Arenin> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_deoxycorticosterone> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/renin> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "\"Treatment is with replacement glucocorticoid therapy; with suppression of DOC secretion, the plasma renin activity, which is suppressed at baseline, increases into the normal range.\" Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 15, p 535  ||  \"Excess DOC secretion eventually leads to hypertension, hypokalemic alkalosis, and suppression of the renin-angiotensin system\" and \"Replacement therapy with physiologic doses of glucocorticoids suppresses DOC and corticosterone secretion and normalizes serum potassium levels, blood pressure, and plasma renin and aldosterone levels\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 23, p 905–906"
    ; pmo:mechanism "DOC exerts mineralocorticoid-mediated volume expansion, which suppresses the juxtaglomerular apparatus and renin secretion (mineralocorticoid suppression of renin)"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/cyp11b1_activity> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_11_deoxycortisol> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Acyp11b1_activity%3Anegative%3Aplasma_11_deoxycortisol> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/cyp11b1_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_11_deoxycortisol> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "\"The condition arises because of mutations in the 11β-hydroxylase (CYP11B1) gene that result in loss of enzyme activity and a block in the conversion of 11-deoxycortisol to cortisol. ... the diagnosis can be made by measuring a plasma synacthen–stimulated 11-deoxycortisol value, which will be greater than 52 nmol/L\" Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 15, p 534–535"
    ; pmo:mechanism "CYP11B1 (11β-hydroxylase) converts 11-deoxycortisol to cortisol; LoF blocks this conversion, causing 11-deoxycortisol to accumulate"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_estrone> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/pituitary_lh_secretion> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aplasma_estrone%3Anegative%3Apituitary_lh_secretion> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_estrone> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/pituitary_lh_secretion> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "\"Hypogonadotropic hypogonadism in male patients is a consequence of increased aromatization of adrenal androgens, in particular androstenedione to estrone, resulting in suppression of pituitary LH and FSH secretion. The condition is reversible after optimization of glucocorticoid therapy.\" Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 15, p 533"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Estrone (and estrogens generally) provide negative feedback at the pituitary gonadotrope, suppressing LH secretion; high estrone from peripheral aromatization mimics central estrogen feedback"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_estrone> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/pituitary_fsh_secretion> .
