<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aaldosterone%3Apositive%3Aextracellular_fluid_volume> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/aldosterone> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/extracellular_fluid_volume> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "\"Excess aldosterone secretion causes hypertension through two main mechanisms: mineralocorticoid-induced expansion of plasma and extracellular fluid volume and increased total peripheral vascular resistance.\" Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 16, p 1355-1358"
    ; pmo:mechanism "excess aldosterone secretion causes expansion of plasma and extracellular fluid volume via mineralocorticoid-driven sodium and water retention"
    .
