    ; dcterms:source "\"Excess aldosterone secretion causes hypertension through two main mechanisms: mineralocorticoid-induced expansion of plasma and extracellular fluid volume and increased total peripheral vascular resistance.\" Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 16, p 1355-1358"
    ; pmo:mechanism "chronic excess aldosterone increases total peripheral vascular resistance, contributing to hypertension independent of volume expansion"
    .
