    ; pmo:causalEvidence "perturbation"
    ; dcterms:source "\"A critical component of the reawakening of the GnRH neuronal network is the increase ... in KISS1 mRNA expression in kisspeptinergic neurons in the medial basal hypothalamus and the secretion of kisspeptins, the cognate ligands for the kisspeptin receptor (KISS1R, formerly GPR54) on the surface of the GnRH neuron (Shahab et al). As a consequence, the amplitude and, to a lesser extent, the frequency of GnRH pulses increase\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 26, p. 1041 (citing Shahab M et al. Proc Natl Acad Sci USA 2005;102:2129–2134, increased hypothalamic GPR54 signaling in primates reactivates GnRH pulse generator)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "kisspeptin binds KISS1R (GPR54) on GnRH neuron surface → increases amplitude and frequency of GnRH pulses"
    .
