    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "\"Postheparin hepatic lipase activity is increased by exogenous androgens (and decreased by estrogens), accounting for the decrease in HDL after androgen treatment\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 26, p. 1600"
    ; pmo:mechanism "estrogens decrease hepatic lipase activity → reduced HDL catabolism → increased HDL-cholesterol"
    .
