    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "\"hemoglobin levels increase at puberty in boys; the effect appears to be mediated by androgen, as treatment of boys with CDP with testosterone and letrozole (to block aromatization to estrogen) resulted in increased hemoglobin levels, even in the absence of a rise in IGF1\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 26, p. 1038"
    ; pmo:mechanism "androgen treatment raises hemoglobin levels; effect mediated by androgen (independent of IGF1 rise)"
    .
