<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Akisspeptin_hypothalamic%3Apositive%3Agnrh> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/kisspeptin_hypothalamic> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/gnrh> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "\"Mice transfected with mutant KISS1R genes exhibited hypogonadotropic hypogonadism, although they had normal content of GnRH in their hypothalamus and were responsive to GnRH\" and \"hypogonadotropic hypogonadism and CPP occur with different mutations of KISS1R\" Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 26, p 1064-1065"
    ; pmo:mechanism "kisspeptin binding KISS1R on GnRH neurons stimulates GnRH release; loss-of-function KISS1R mutations cause hypogonadotropic hypogonadism; gain-of-function KISS1R mutations cause central precocious puberty"
    .
