    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "During puberty, leptin continued to rise in girls, whereas in boys, the leptin mean levels peaked at Tanner stage 2 and decreased to prepubertal concentrations by genital stage 5. This decrease is attributed to the effect of testosterone on leptin secretion. Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 26"
    ; pmo:mechanism "testosterone suppresses leptin secretion from adipose tissue; as pubertal boys progress, leptin levels decrease coincident with rising testosterone"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hypothalamic_gabaergic_tone> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/gnrh_neuron_gnrh_secretion> .
