    ; dcterms:source "\"Administration of the somatostatin analogue octreotide leads to a decrease in basal ghrelin values and some decrease in values after meals\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 26, p. 1097"
    ; pmo:mechanism "somatostatin (via SST receptor activation on gastric ghrelin cells) suppresses ghrelin secretion; shown directly by octreotide (long-acting somatostatin analogue) administration in Prader-Willi syndrome patients"
    .
