    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "\"Gonadal steroids increase plasma IGF1 concentrations in CPP, as in normal puberty.\" and \"Treatment with GnRH agonist reduces the level of IGF1 to the normal range for bone age but not for chronologic age.\" Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 26, p. 1134"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Testosterone (as gonadal steroid) increases circulating IGF-1; GnRH agonist suppression of testosterone in CPP boys reduces IGF-1 concentrations"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/cyp17a1_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/leydig_testosterone_secretion> .
