    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "\"Ketoconazole, an orally active substituted imidazole derivative, suppresses gonadal and adrenal biosynthesis by inhibiting the enzyme CYP17, which regulates both 17-hydroxylation and the scission (17,20-lyase) of 17α-hydroxypregnenolone (Δ5-17P) to DHEA\" and \"secretion, testosterone secretion, height velocity and rate of bone maturation, and aggressive and hyperactive behavior have reportedly been decreased by treatment with oral medroxyprogesterone acetate\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 26, p 1142–1143"
    ; pmo:mechanism "CYP17A1 17,20-lyase catalyses androgen precursor (17-OH-pregnenolone → DHEA) supply for Leydig-cell testosterone biosynthesis; ketoconazole inhibition of CYP17 suppresses testosterone production in testotoxicosis boys"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/trh> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/pituitary_fsh_secretion> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Atrh%3Apositive%3Apituitary_fsh_secretion> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/trh> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/pituitary_fsh_secretion> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "pharmacological"
    ; dcterms:source "\"administration of TRH appears to increase FSH release in normal children (but not in adults). Moreover, the FSH response to TRH, but not GnRH, is augmented in primary hypothyroidism\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 26, p 1152"
    ; pmo:mechanism "TRH stimulates pituitary gonadotrophs to release FSH (in addition to thyrotrophs); effect is augmented in primary hypothyroidism; chronic hypothyroidism increases TRH → elevated FSH → ovarian follicular cysts and incomplete sexual precocity"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/adrenal_hsd3b2_activity> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_dhea> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aadrenal_hsd3b2_activity%3Anegative%3Aplasma_dhea> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/adrenal_hsd3b2_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_dhea> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "curated_mechanistic"
    ; dcterms:source "\"A rise in intra-adrenal cortisol may inhibit 3βHSD activity, thereby increasing DHEA according to in vitro evidence.\" Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 26, p 1162"
    ; pmo:mechanism "HSD3B2 converts DHEA (Δ5 substrate) to androstenedione (Δ4); when HSD3B2 is inhibited, DHEA accumulates"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/sult2a1_activity> obo:RO_0002305 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_androstenedione> .
