    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "\"androstenedione was high owing to inadequate formation of DHEAS that decreases the conversion of DHEA to androstenedione\" Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 26, p 1163"
    ; pmo:mechanism "SULT2A1-mediated DHEA sulfation competes with DHEA→androstenedione conversion; when SULT2A1 is non-functional (PAPSS2 LoF), DHEA flows to androstenedione instead, raising plasma androstenedione"
    .
