    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "\"Leptin absence, resulting from gene mutations, is associated with absent appetite control resulting in morbid obesity in mice, rats, and humans\" and \"the handful of individuals with leptin deficiency can be treated with exogenous leptin, which normalizes weight and food intake\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 40, p 1570"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Leptin receptor signalling in hypothalamic POMC neurons suppresses appetite; loss of signalling leads to hyperphagia"
    .
