    ; pmo:mechanism "Osteoclastic bone resorption degrades bone-type-I collagen; galactosyl-hydroxylysine (a collagen-unique, non-reutilized hydroxylysine glycoside enriched in bone) is liberated and excreted -> higher osteoclast resorption activity -> higher galactosyl-hydroxylysine output (sign +)."
