    ; pmo:causalEvidence "mechanistic_model"
    ; dcterms:source "Adlung et al. (2021) Cell Reports 36:109507, PubMed 34380040 (STAT5 sets the survival threshold of erythroid progenitor cells); the calibrated model is BioModels BIOMD0000001077 (intervention-capable: nuclear pSTAT5 of 24-118 molecules for 120 min ensures CFU-E survival). Genetic-LoF converse: Socolovsky et al. (1999) Cell 98:181, PubMed 10428030 (Stat5a-/-5b-/- -> erythroid progenitor apoptosis, fetal anemia). Boron & Boulpaep, Medical Physiology. [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "nuclear pSTAT5 activates the erythroid survival/proliferation transcriptional program (quality: pSTAT5 activity -> disposition: promoter occupancy at target genes -> process: transcription of proliferation/survival genes -> quality: progenitor proliferation/survival rate)"
    .
