    ; dcterms:source "Primary genetic loss-of-function: Socolovsky et al. (1999) Cell 98:181, PubMed 10428030 (opened) — Stat5a-/-5b-/- knockout abolishes immediate-early Bcl-xL induction in erythroid cells and STAT5 binds the Bcl-X promoter directly, i.e. do(STAT5 LoF) -> Bcl-xL down. Adlung et al. (2021) Cell Reports 36:109507 (STAT5-driven anti-apoptotic survival program in erythroid progenitors). Boron & Boulpaep, Medical Physiology (EPO promotes erythroid survival). [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "pSTAT5 transcriptionally induces the anti-apoptotic gene Bcl-xL (quality: pSTAT5 activity -> disposition: STAT5 binding at the BCL2L1 promoter -> process: Bcl-xL transcription -> quality: Bcl-xL protein level)"
    .
