<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/island_macrophage_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/erythroblast_proliferation> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aisland_macrophage_activity%3Apositive%3Aerythroblast_proliferation> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/island_macrophage_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/erythroblast_proliferation> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "perturbation"
    ; dcterms:source "Interventional: erythroblasts in direct macrophage contact proliferate ~3-fold more than progenitors cultured alone (EPO-independent, altered G0/G1 transit), and chemical depletion of splenic macrophages prevents the appropriate erythroid response to bleeding — do(macrophage support up/down) shifts erythroblast proliferation. Chasis & Mohandas (2008) Blood 112:470-478, PMID 18650462 (full text). OmniPath ligrec KITLG->KIT is_stimulation=True, PMID 7680037; Manwani & Bieker (2008) Curr Top Dev Biol 82:23-53, PMID 18282516. Boron & Boulpaep, Medical Physiology. [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "paracrine/juxtacrine: macrophage membrane-bound SCF (KITLG) engages erythroblast KIT receptor tyrosine kinase (quality: macrophage support activity -> disposition: KITLG presentation + VCAM1 adhesion -> process: KIT signaling, GO:0038109 KIT-signaling-pathway -> quality: erythroblast proliferation rate)"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/island_macrophage_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/erythroblast_maturation> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aisland_macrophage_activity%3Apositive%3Aerythroblast_maturation> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/island_macrophage_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/erythroblast_maturation> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "perturbation"
    ; dcterms:source "Interventional: macrophage depletion causes pro-erythroblast differentiation arrest, i.e. do(macrophage down) impairs terminal maturation/enucleation; macrophage contact (VCAM1-VLA4 adhesion, iron/ferritin handoff) supports hemoglobinization and enucleation. Chasis & Mohandas (2008) Blood 112:470-478, PMID 18650462 (full text). OmniPath ligrec VCAM1->ITGA4 is_stimulation=True; 22623428; Manwani & Bieker (2008) Curr Top Dev Biol 82:23-53, PMID 18282516. Boron & Boulpaep, Medical Physiology. [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "juxtacrine adhesion + iron handoff: macrophage VCAM1 binds erythroblast integrin alpha4-beta1 (VLA-4) anchoring the cell and supplying iron/ferritin for hemoglobinization (quality: macrophage support activity -> disposition: VCAM1-VLA4 adhesion + iron supply -> process: GO:0043249 erythrocyte maturation / enucleation -> quality: erythroblast maturation rate)"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/erythroblast_proliferation> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/island_macrophage_activity> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aerythroblast_proliferation%3Apositive%3Aisland_macrophage_activity> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/erythroblast_proliferation> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/island_macrophage_activity> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; dcterms:source "OmniPath ligrec ICAM4->ITGAV is_stimulation=True, PMID 11435317 (15355350); Chasis & Mohandas (2008) Blood 112:470-478, PMID 18650462. Manwani & Bieker (2008) PMID 18282516. [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "juxtacrine feedback: expanding erythroblasts present ICAM4 to macrophage alphaV integrin, assembling/stabilizing the island and sustaining macrophage support (quality: erythroblast number/proliferation -> disposition: ICAM4-alphaV adhesion -> process: GO:0007157 heterophilic cell-cell adhesion / island assembly -> quality: macrophage support activity)"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/erythroblast_maturation> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/island_macrophage_activity> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aerythroblast_maturation%3Apositive%3Aisland_macrophage_activity> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/erythroblast_maturation> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/island_macrophage_activity> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; dcterms:source "Chasis & Mohandas (2008) Blood 112:470-478, PMID 18650462 (central macrophage ingests extruded nuclei); Manwani & Bieker (2008) Curr Top Dev Biol 82:23-53, PMID 18282516. [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "erythroblast enucleation releases pyrenocytes (extruded nuclei) presenting phosphatidylserine, engaging macrophage clearance receptors that reinforce the nurse program (quality: erythroblast maturation/enucleation rate -> disposition: PS exposure + ICAM4-alphaV contact -> process: GO:0006911 phagocytosis of pyrenocytes -> quality: macrophage support activity)"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/erythroblast_proliferation> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/erythroblast_maturation> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aerythroblast_proliferation%3Apositive%3Aerythroblast_maturation> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/erythroblast_proliferation> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/erythroblast_maturation> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; dcterms:source "Manwani & Bieker (2008) Curr Top Dev Biol 82:23-53, PMID 18282516; Boron & Boulpaep, Medical Physiology (erythroid precursors proliferate then mature/enucleate). [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "lineage progression: a larger proliferating erythroblast pool feeds the terminal maturation/enucleation program (quality: erythroblast proliferation rate -> disposition: cell-cycle exit competence -> process: GO:0030218 erythrocyte differentiation -> quality: erythroblast maturation/enucleation rate)"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/island_macrophage_activity> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/erythroid_progenitor_proliferation> .
