    ; dcterms:source "OmniPath ligrec IFNG->IFNGR1/IFNGR2 consensus_stimulation=True (refs SIGNOR:10986460; Macrophage:7617032) | textbook corroboration: OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-119 (21.4: The Adaptive Immune Response - T Lymphocytes and Their Functional Types): 'Th1 cells secrete cytokines that regulate the immunological activity and development of a variety of cells, including macrophages and other types of T cells.'; OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology 2e §anp-121 (21.6: The Immune Response Against Pathogens): 'infected macrophages receiving cytokine signals from Th1 cells turn on special metabolic pathways' including oxidative killing of intracellular bacteria.; OpenStax Biology 2e §bio-42.2 (42.2: Adaptive Immune Response): 'TH1 cells secrete cytokines to enhance the activities of macrophages and other T cells' and 'stimulated T cells secrete specific cytokines that send feedback to the macrophage to stimulate its digestive capabilities' [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Th1 IFN-gamma -> IFNGR1/IFNGR2 on macrophage -> JAK1/JAK2 -> STAT1 -> classical (M1) activation (GO:0060333 IFN-gamma-mediated signaling pathway)"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/macrophage_activation> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/th17_cell_activation> .
