<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Atreg_il10_secretion%3Anegative%3Amacrophage_activation> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/treg_il10_secretion> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/macrophage_activation> ; pmo:sign "-"
    ; dcterms:source "OmniPath ligrec IL10->IL10RA/IL10RB consensus_stimulation=True for receptor binding; functional inhibition of macrophage activation; Janeway's Immunobiology 9th ed. | textbook corroboration: OpenStax Biology 2e §bio-42.2 (42.2: Adaptive Immune Response): 'regulatory T (Treg) cells, specialized lymphocytes that suppress local inflammation and inhibit the secretion of stimulatory immune factors' — Treg IL-10 suppresses macrophage pro-inflammatory activity [citations PubMed-verified]"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Treg IL-10 -> IL10RA/IL10RB on macrophage -> STAT3 -> suppression of NF-kB-driven pro-inflammatory cytokine (TNF/IL-6/IL-12) transcription (GO:0032613 IL-10 production / GO:0050728 negative regulation of inflammatory response)"
    .
