    ; pmo:mechanism "macula densa ATP -> P2X/P2Y and adenosine -> ADORA1 on extraglomerular mesangial cell -> Gi/Go-PLC -> IP3 -> intracellular Ca2+ rise -> mesangial/contractile activation (GO:0006816 calcium ion transport)"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/eg_mesangial_contraction> obo:RO_0002304 <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/afferent_arteriolar_tone> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/causal/influence%3Aeg_mesangial_contraction%3Apositive%3Aafferent_arteriolar_tone> a pmo:CausalRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/eg_mesangial_contraction> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/afferent_arteriolar_tone> ; pmo:sign "+"
    ; pmo:causalEvidence "genetic_lof_gof"
    ; dcterms:source "Moller, Jacobsen, Holstein-Rathlou & Sorensen, Front Physiol 2020;11:961, PMID:32848881: connexin40 (and connexin45) knockout mice show significantly reduced local and conducted vasoconstrictor responses in afferent arterioles, demonstrating that Cx40/Cx45 gap-junction coupling is required for propagating a contractile signal to afferent arteriolar smooth muscle (genetic loss-of-function of the gap-junction connexin blunts the target response; stimulus was electrical in the isolated perfused nephron preparation, not mesangial-cell-specific). Wagner et al. Circ Res 2007;100:556-563 (Cx40 essential for pressure control of renin; couples JG/mesangial/vascular cells); Schnermann & Briggs Kidney Int 2008 (TGF Ca2+ wave -> afferent vasoconstriction)."
    ; pmo:mechanism "extraglomerular mesangial Ca2+ wave propagates via connexin-40 (Cx40/GJA5) gap junctions to afferent arteriolar smooth muscle -> contraction (GO:0007267 cell-cell signaling; juxtacrine/gap-junction)"
    .
