<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/production/64> a pmo:ProductionRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/parafollicular_cell_calcitonin_secretion> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_calcitonin> ; pmo:sign "+" ; pmo:productionEvidence "curated_source_statement"
    ; dcterms:source "\"Calcitonin is found in the nonfollicular cells of the thyroid, called C cells\" and \"a linear relationship between the secretion of calcitonin and ambient calcium levels\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 29"
    ; pmo:mechanism "thyroid C-cell secretory disposition -> exocytosis of calcitonin -> rise in plasma calcitonin concentration"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/aanat_activity> pmo:produces <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_melatonin> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/production/65> a pmo:ProductionRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/aanat_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_melatonin> ; pmo:sign "+" ; pmo:productionEvidence "curated_source_statement"
    ; dcterms:source "\"it is released into the blood or CSF directly after its biosynthesis in proportion to AANAT activity\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 7, p 125"
    ; pmo:mechanism "AANAT is the rate-limiting enzyme of pineal melatonin biosynthesis; melatonin is released directly after synthesis in proportion to AANAT catalytic activity"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/type_1_deiodinase_activity> pmo:produces <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/free_t3> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/production/66> a pmo:ProductionRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/type_1_deiodinase_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/free_t3> ; pmo:sign "+" ; pmo:productionEvidence "curated_source_statement"
    ; dcterms:source "\"T4 is activated by monodeiodination of the phenolic thyronine ring by D1 or D2 to form T3\" and \"D1 is largely responsible for the production of T3 that escapes from the cells, especially liver and kidney, into the circulation\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 11 / ch 23"
    ; pmo:mechanism "DIO1 (D1) outer-ring (5') monodeiodination of T4 yields T3; D1 is largely responsible for T3 that escapes cells (liver/kidney) into the circulation, raising circulating free T3"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/type_2_deiodinase_activity> pmo:produces <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/free_t3> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/production/67> a pmo:ProductionRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/type_2_deiodinase_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/free_t3> ; pmo:sign "+" ; pmo:productionEvidence "curated_source_statement"
    ; dcterms:source "\"The type 2 outer-ring monodeiodinase (D2)... It deiodinates T4 to T3 and rT3 to T2\" and \"D2 is responsible for the production of local tissue T3\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 23, p 842"
    ; pmo:mechanism "DIO2 (D2) outer-ring deiodination of T4 produces T3; in humans D2 contributes substantially to the circulating free-T3 pool in addition to local tissue T3"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/type_2_deiodinase_activity> pmo:produces <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/free_t4> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/production/68> a pmo:ProductionRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/type_2_deiodinase_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/free_t4> ; pmo:sign "-" ; pmo:productionEvidence "curated_source_statement"
    ; dcterms:source "\"The type 2 outer-ring monodeiodinase (D2)... It deiodinates T4 to T3 and rT3 to T2\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 23, p 842"
    ; pmo:mechanism "DIO2 consumes T4 as substrate during outer-ring deiodination (T4->T3), depleting free T4 (substrate-consumption production edge, negative sign for the consumed pool)"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/type_3_deiodinase_activity> pmo:produces <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/free_t4> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/production/69> a pmo:ProductionRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/type_3_deiodinase_activity> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/free_t4> ; pmo:sign "-" ; pmo:productionEvidence "curated_source_statement"
    ; dcterms:source "\"Type 3 monodeiodinase (D3) inactivates T4 and T3 via inner-ring deiodination of T4 to rT3 and of T3 to T2\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 23, p 842"
    ; pmo:mechanism "DIO3 inner-ring deiodination converts T4 to inactive reverse-T3, consuming T4 and lowering free T4 (substrate-consumption production edge)"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/osteocyte_fgf23_secretion> pmo:produces <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/fgf23> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/production/70> a pmo:ProductionRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/osteocyte_fgf23_secretion> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/fgf23> ; pmo:sign "+" ; pmo:productionEvidence "curated_source_statement"
    ; dcterms:source "\"FGF23, produced exclusively by osteocytes and osteoblasts\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 31, p 1312"
    ; pmo:mechanism "osteocyte secretory disposition -> FGF23 release into circulation -> plasma FGF23 rises"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/beta_cell_insulin_secretion> pmo:produces <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_amylin> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/production/71> a pmo:ProductionRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/beta_cell_insulin_secretion> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_amylin> ; pmo:sign "+" ; pmo:productionEvidence "curated_source_statement"
    ; dcterms:source "\"Amylin, or islet amyloid polypeptide (IAPP)... is cosecreted with insulin from pancre[atic beta cells]\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 39, p 1566"
    ; pmo:mechanism "amylin (IAPP) is packaged in the same beta-cell secretory granules as insulin and cosecreted by the same nutrient-stimulated exocytosis; the beta-cell insulin secretion rate indexes the shared secretory output that raises plasma amylin"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/theca_androstenedione_secretion> pmo:produces <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_androstenedione> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/production/72> a pmo:ProductionRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/theca_androstenedione_secretion> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_androstenedione> ; pmo:sign "+" ; pmo:productionEvidence "curated_source_statement"
    ; dcterms:source "\"LH stimulates androstenedione production in theca cells of the ovary\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 17, p 593"
    ; pmo:mechanism "ovarian theca-cell steroidogenic secretion of androstenedione (LH-driven C19 output) raises plasma androstenedione"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepatocyte_shbg_secretion> pmo:produces <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_shbg> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/production/73> a pmo:ProductionRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/hepatocyte_shbg_secretion> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_shbg> ; pmo:sign "+" ; pmo:productionEvidence "curated_source_statement"
    ; dcterms:source "\"SHBG, which is synthesized by hepatocytes of the liver\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed., ch 19, p 685"
    ; pmo:mechanism "hepatocyte synthesis and secretion of SHBG sets the circulating SHBG pool"
    .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/zona_reticularis_dheas_secretion> pmo:produces <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_dheas> .
<https://w3id.org/physiomap/edge/production/74> a pmo:ProductionRelation ; pmo:hasSource <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/zona_reticularis_dheas_secretion> ; pmo:hasTarget <https://w3id.org/physiomap/node/plasma_dheas> ; pmo:sign "+" ; pmo:productionEvidence "curated_source_statement"
    ; dcterms:source "CB-PHY-006 (production lift, adrenal zona reticularis -> plasma DHEA-S). SULT2A1 is localized to the zona reticularis and sulfates DHEA at C3beta to DHEA-S, quantitatively the dominant adrenal secretory steroid (~95-100% adrenal origin): PAPSS2/SULT2A1 adrenal DHEA-sulfation coupling, PMC6016456. \"DHEA-S is secreted by the adrenal zona reticularis; adrenarche = maturation of the zona reticularis with rising DHEAS\" — Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, 14th ed. (ISBN:9780323297387). Structural mirror of the deployed zona_glomerulosa_cell_aldosterone_secretion -> aldosterone production edge."
    ; pmo:mechanism "adrenal zona reticularis cells sulfate DHEA intracellularly via SULT2A1 (DHEA-preferring sulfotransferase) and secrete DHEA-sulfate; the zona reticularis secretion rate sets the plasma DHEA-S pool. Produced entity is the sulfated ester DHEA-S (CHEBI:16814), NOT DHEA (CHEBI:28689) — no conflation"
    .
