    ; dcterms:source "\"A simplified form of the alveolar gas equation is [PAO2 = PIO2 - PACO2/R] where F is a small correction factor ... which we can ignore.\" (West's Respiratory Physiology, 11th ed., ch 5, Hypoventilation)"
    ; pmo:mechanism "Alveolar gas equation (steady state): PAO2 = PIO2 - PACO2/R (+ small correction F). For fixed inspired PO2 and respiratory exchange ratio R: d(PAO2)/d(PIO2) = +1 and d(PAO2)/d(PACO2) = -1/R < 0."
